UID:20260421T153000Z-2236958@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260421T153000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,800,640/28783_02_RM_Resized_for_web.rev.1761655589.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages,Lectures, talk
 s, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Rhonda and Anthony Moravec Gallery\, Center for Prints\, Drawi
 ngs\, and Photographs\, Third Floor  In this hour-long gallery conversatio
 n\, each guest brings their own perspective to the work and opens up new w
 ays of seeing it together.  Featured guests:Beth Buggenhagen is a Professo
 r of Anthropology at Indiana University. She writes about visual culture\,
  value\, gender\, and Islam in contemporary West Africa\, and is the autho
 r of The Future is in Your Hands: Portrait Photography from Senegal. Her r
 esearch draws on long-term ethnographic work in Senegal and spans photogra
 phy\, material culture\, and global circulation.Leticia Pardo is an Assist
 ant Professor of Architecture at Indiana University's Eskenazi School of A
 rt\, Architecture + Design. She is an architectural designer and multidisc
 iplinary artist whose work explores how place making\, migration\, and bor
 ders inform our built environments. She previously served as Creative Dire
 ctor of Exhibition Design at the Art Institute of Chicago.  Facilitated by
  Leila Reichert\, Curator of Contemporary Art and Laura Scheper\, Interpre
 tation and Volunteer Experiences Manager.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260406T142348Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2236958-in-front-of-the-work-a-g
 allery-dialogue
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="font-claude-response-body break-wor
 ds whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">  Rhonda and Anthony Moravec Gallery\,
  Center for Prints\, Drawings\, and Photographs\, Third Floor</p><p class=
 "font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">  
 In this hour-long gallery conversation\, each guest brings their own persp
 ective to the work and opens up new ways of seeing it together.</p><p clas
 s="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">
   Featured guests:</p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whit
 espace-normal leading-[1.7]"><strong>Beth Buggenhagen</strong> is a Profes
 sor of Anthropology at Indiana University. She writes about visual culture
 \, value\, gender\, and Islam in contemporary West Africa\, and is the aut
 hor of <em>The Future is in Your Hands: Portrait Photography from Senegal<
 /em>. Her research draws on long-term ethnographic work in Senegal and spa
 ns photography\, material culture\, and global circulation.</p><p class="f
 ont-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]"><str
 ong>Leticia Pardo</strong> is an Assistant Professor of Architecture at In
 diana University's Eskenazi School of Art\, Architecture + Design. She is 
 an architectural designer and multidisciplinary artist whose work explores
  how place making\, migration\, and borders inform our built environments.
  She previously served as Creative Director of Exhibition Design at the Ar
 t Institute of Chicago.</p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words
  whitespace-normal leading-[1.7]">  Facilitated by Leila Reichert\, Curato
 r of Contemporary Art and Laura Scheper\, Interpretation and Volunteer Exp
 eriences Manager.</p>
