X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/mooch-the-magnificent/?instance_id=94937", "Bloomington Arts": "https://tockify.com/bloomington.arts.calendar/detail/2122/1776814200000"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/mooch-the-magnificent/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wfhb
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Arts, WFHB Community Calendar
SUMMARY:Mooch the Magnificent
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260421T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260421T193000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020832Z
UID:ai1ec-148418@wfhb.org
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260421T193000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Stages Bloomington\; (812) 727-4950\; info@stagesbloomington.com\;
  https://www.stagesbloomington.org/
DESCRIPTION:Bridges MAYO\, Reimagining Opera for Kids\, and Stages Bloomin
 gton have teamed up to produce Lauren Bernofsky’s “Mooch the Magnifice
 nt\,” with stage director Andrew Keeler and musical director Dr. Lauren 
 Bernofsky. Youth singers and instrumentalists\, ages 8-18\, have been rehe
 arsing alongside professional Reimagining Opera for Kids opera singers\, I
 U Jacobs and community musicians to share a tale about a zookeeper\, Orlan
 do\, and his assistant\, Mooch. Scored for full orchestra and singers\, se
 e what happens when Mooch helps the mechanical animals to disconnect on Tu
 esday\, April 21 at 7:30PM at Fairview Elementary School gym!\n\n“When t
 he cleverest person in the room is … the girl. MOOCH THE MAGNIFICENT is 
 a 40-minute opera on a libretto by Scott Russell Sanders. The setting is a
  zoo of the future\, populated not by animals but by robots in animal form
 . Mooch\, an orphan girl\, convinces the zookeeper to hire her to fix the 
 robots when they break down\, but she secretly reprograms them to be incre
 asingly wild.”
LOCATION:Fairview Elementary 500 W 7th St\, Bloomington
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/mooch-the-magnificent/
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//
 EN'>\n<HTML>\n<HEAD>\n<TITLE></TITLE>\n</HEAD>\n<BODY><div class='gmail_de
 fault'>Bridges MAYO\, Reimagining Opera for Kids\, and Stages Bloomington 
 have teamed up to produce Lauren Bernofsky’s “Mooch the Magnificent\,
 ” with stage director Andrew Keeler and musical director Dr. Lauren Bern
 ofsky. Youth singers and instrumentalists\, ages 8-18\, have been rehearsi
 ng alongside professional Reimagining Opera for Kids opera singers\, IU Ja
 cobs and community musicians to share a tale about a zookeeper\, Orlando\,
  and his assistant\, Mooch. Scored for full orchestra and singers\, see wh
 at happens when Mooch helps the mechanical animals to disconnect on Tuesda
 y\, April 21 at 7:30PM at Fairview Elementary School gym!</div>\n<div></di
 v>\n<div>“When the cleverest person in the room is … the girl. MOOCH T
 HE MAGNIFICENT is a 40-minute opera on a libretto by Scott Russell Sanders
 . The setting is a zoo of the future\, populated not by animals but by rob
 ots in animal form. Mooch\, an orphan girl\, convinces the zookeeper to hi
 re her to fix the robots when they break down\, but she secretly reprogram
 s them to be increasingly wild.”</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
