BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/green-drinks-bloomington-common-wealth-living-in-a-shared-world/?instance_id=94903"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/green-drinks-bloomington-common-wealth-living-in-a-shared-world/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wfhb
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
SUMMARY:Green Drinks Bloomington: Common Wealth: Living in a Shared World.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260422T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260422T193000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020832Z
UID:ai1ec-148338@wfhb.org
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260422T173000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:Marcia Veldman\, Green Drinks Bloomington\; 812-325-2446\; marciav
 eldman@gmail.com\; marciaveldman@gmail.com
DESCRIPTION:Green Drinks Bloomington is a lively\, informal social network
 ing event for people from all walks of life who are interested in making a
  greener world. Green Drinks gathers monthly to share libations and dialog
 ue\, explore ideas and make new friends and business connections.\nOn Eart
 h Day\, Wednesday\, April 22 at 6 PM (doors open at 5:30)\, Green Drinks B
 loomington will offer a presentation by Scott Russell Sanders\, Distinguis
 hed Professor Emeritus of English at Indiana University\, and a fellow of 
 the American Academy of Arts and Sciences. He will speak about “Common W
 ealth: Living in a Shared World.” Our wellbeing depends far more on the 
 wealth we share than our private finances and possessions. This talk will 
 celebrate the gifts of nature and culture that support and enrich our live
 s. It will also show how these shared riches—atmosphere\, oceans\, biodi
 versity\, parks and public schools\, arts and science\, laws and language\
 , and many more—are under assault by those who wish to exploit them for 
 personal or corporate gain. By recognizing the common wealth that sustains
  us\, we may be moved to defend it.\nGreen Drinks Bloomington is held the 
 4th Wednesday of the month through October from 5:30 – 7:30 pm at the Up
 land Brewing Company’s Wood Shop venue. Some food will be provided. To r
 eceive a monthly reminder\, write greendrinksbloomington@gmail.com. To lea
 rn more about Green Drinks visit www.greendrinks.org.
LOCATION:Upland Brewing Co. Wood Shop: 350 w. 11th st.
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/green-drinks-bloomington-common-wealth-living-i
 n-a-shared-world/
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//
 EN'>\n<HTML>\n<HEAD>\n<TITLE></TITLE>\n</HEAD>\n<BODY><p>Green Drinks Bloo
 mington is a lively\, informal social networking event for people from all
  walks of life who are interested in making a greener world. Green Drinks 
 gathers monthly to share libations and dialogue\, explore ideas and make n
 ew friends and business connections.</p>\n<p>On Earth Day\, Wednesday\, Ap
 ril 22 at 6 PM (doors open at 5:30)\, Green Drinks Bloomington will offer 
 a presentation by Scott Russell Sanders\, Distinguished Professor Emeritus
  of English at Indiana University\, and a fellow of the American Academy o
 f Arts and Sciences. He will speak about “Common Wealth: Living in a Sha
 red World.” Our wellbeing depends far more on the wealth we share than o
 ur private finances and possessions. This talk will celebrate the gifts of
  nature and culture that support and enrich our lives. It will also show h
 ow these shared riches—atmosphere\, oceans\, biodiversity\, parks and pu
 blic schools\, arts and science\, laws and language\, and many more—are 
 under assault by those who wish to exploit them for personal or corporate 
 gain. By recognizing the common wealth that sustains us\, we may be moved 
 to defend it.</p>\n<p>Green Drinks Bloomington is held the 4th Wednesday o
 f the month through October from 5:30 – 7:30 pm at the Upland Brewing Co
 mpany’s Wood Shop venue. Some food will be provided. To receive a monthl
 y reminder\, write greendrinksbloomington@gmail.com. To learn more about G
 reen Drinks visit www.greendrinks.org.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-COST-TYPE:free
END:VEVENT
