DESCRIPTION:Bio  Mahdi Taraghi is a third-year Ph.D. student in Environmen
 tal Science at the O'Neill School of Public and Environmental Affairs\, In
 diana University Bloomington. He holds a Master's degree in Water Resource
 s Engineering and is passionate about the intersection of environmental po
 licy\, socio-environmental systems\, and complex systems modeling. His res
 earch focuses on the dynamic interplay between human decision-making and e
 nvironmental processes\, using agent-based modeling to investigate complex
  interactions within socio-environmental systems.About the Ostrom Workshop
  Research Series  Learn about innovative research by Graduate Students and
  Visiting Scholars as they advance the mission of the Ostrom Workshop\, bu
 ilding upon the theme of governance to understand and address major societ
 al problems.
