 eight/283/crop/1/src_region/52\,177\,1172\,1234/27550_Taraghi_photo.rev.17
 55119359.jpg 3x" data-max-w="1120" data-max-h="1057" loading="lazy" data-o
 ptimized="true"/></picture></p><p><strong>Bio</strong></p><p>  Mahdi Tarag
 hi is a third-year Ph.D. student in Environmental Science at the O'Neill S
 chool of Public and Environmental Affairs\, Indiana University Bloomington
 . He holds a Master's degree in Water Resources Engineering and is passion
 ate about the intersection of environmental policy\, socio-environmental s
 ystems\, and complex systems modeling. His research focuses on the dynamic
  interplay between human decision-making and environmental processes\, usi
 ng agent-based modeling to investigate complex interactions within socio-e
 nvironmental systems.</p><p><strong>About the Ostrom Workshop Research Ser
 ies</strong></p><p>  Learn about innovative research by Graduate Students 
 and Visiting Scholars as they advance the mission of the Ostrom Workshop\,
  building upon the theme of governance to understand and address major soc
 ietal problems.</p>
