X-SOURCE-ID:iu_arts_humanities
X-SOURCE:IU Arts & Humanities Institute
SUMMARY:Meet the Author: Justin Garcia
DTSTART:20260423T200000Z
DTEND:20260423T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260409T153320Z
UID:20260423T200000Z-2263940@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260423T200000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/130/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/486,748,2675,2937/30870_MTA_Justin_Garcia_square.rev.17757790
 37.jpg
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Intimacy is central to the human condition\, a key pillar of a
  loving relationship\, and the most powerful need that drives our species.
  But therein lies the challenge. We evolved to crave both emotional intima
 cy and sexual intimacy\, yet these impulses are often at odds. In The Inti
 mate Animal\, Garcia reveals how our evolved need for intimacy animates th
 e full life cycle of the romantic relationship\, from the thrill of first 
 attraction to the devotion that lasts decades. Whether you're seeking that
  special someone\, recovering from heartbreak\, or trying to keep the pass
 ion alive\, this is the essential\, research-backed guide to forging deepe
 r\, more intimate connections in these disconnected times.Dr. Justin Garci
 a is Executive Director and Senior Scientist at the Kinsey Institute\, Rut
 h N. Halls Professor in the College of Arts and Sciences\, and Founding Co
 -Director of Human Sexuality and Health at the IU School of Medicine. He h
 as consulted with a variety of industry partners and is currently the Chie
 f Scientific Advisor to Match\, where he provides expertise for the annual
  Singles in America study. His research has been featured widely in the me
 dia\, focusing on people's romantic and sexual lives throughout the life c
 ourse.  For accommodation requests\, please email cahi@iu.edu.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260413T144123Z
LOCATION:Maxwell Hall - Room Number: Grand Hall
URL:https://events.iu.edu/cahi/event/2263940-meet-the-author-justin-garcia
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<div>  Intimacy is central to the human condi
 tion\, a key pillar of a loving relationship\, and the most powerful need 
 that drives our species. But therein lies the challenge. We evolved to cra
 ve both emotional intimacy and sexual intimacy\, yet these impulses are of
 ten at odds. In <i>The Intimate Animal</i>\, Garcia reveals how our evolve
 d need for intimacy animates the full life cycle of the romantic relations
 hip\, from the thrill of first attraction to the devotion that lasts decad
 es. Whether you're seeking that special someone\, recovering from heartbre
 ak\, or trying to keep the passion alive\, this is the essential\, researc
 h-backed guide to forging deeper\, more intimate connections in these disc
 onnected times.</div><div></div><div><strong>Dr. Justin Garcia</strong> is
  Executive Director and Senior Scientist at the Kinsey Institute\, Ruth N.
  Halls Professor in the College of Arts and Sciences\, and Founding Co-Dir
 ector of Human Sexuality and Health at the IU School of Medicine. He has c
 onsulted with a variety of industry partners and is currently the Chief Sc
 ientific Advisor to Match\, where he provides expertise for the annual Sin
 gles in America study. His research has been featured widely in the media\
 , focusing on people's romantic and sexual lives throughout the life cours
 e.</div><div></div><div>  For accommodation requests\, please email cahi@i
 u.edu.</div>
