SUMMARY:Arbor Day Tree Planting at Rogers Family Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T120000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020748Z
UID:2skfsjt3dj05jtei84j5migmi3@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T090000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20251118T155232Z
DESCRIPTION:<h3><span>Celebrate Arbor Day in Indiana on the last Friday in
  April and continue Bloomington's tree-planting tradition! </span></h3><p
 ><strong>Friday\, April 24 from 9 a.m.-noon at </strong><a href="/node/512
 "><strong>Rogers Family Park</strong></a><strong>\, 2000 E. Winslow Rd. in
  Bloomington</strong></p><p>Assist Parks and Recreation urban forestry sta
 ff as they plant trees along the Jackson Creek Trail\, and take home a fre
 e tree seedling while supplies last. Tree planting volunteers will help di
 g and widen holes to plant balled and burlapped trees\, move trees into pl
 anting position\, and spread mulch. Volunteers ages 14 yrs. and older are 
 welcome! </p><p>Gloves and shovels are provided\; meet at the red barn at
  Rogers Family Park. Vehicle parking is available inside the entrance to R
 ogers Family Park south of the Winslow-High-Rogers roundabout. Additional 
 vehicle parking is available at Sherwood Oaks Park and at Olcott Park.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251118T155233Z
LOCATION:Rogers Family Park\, 2000 E Winslow Rd\, Bloomington\, IN 47401\,
  USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
