BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/the-museum-in-question-an-inside-look-at-two-new-iu-exhibitions/?instance_id=92912"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/the-museum-in-question-an-inside-look-at-two-new-iu-exhibitions/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wfhb
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
SUMMARY:The Museum in Question: An Inside Look at Two New IU Exhibitions
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T163000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020832Z
UID:ai1ec-144514@wfhb.org
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T130000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:How do museums differ from classrooms\, publications\, and oth
 er learning media? What do museum people want their visitors to learn and 
 feel—and what preconceptions help or hinder visitors from meeting those 
 expectations? Eric Sandweiss\, Thomas and Kathryn Miller Professor of Hist
 ory\, offers an insider’s look at two exciting new IU exhibitions that a
 llows us to hear how museum people think—and to respond for ourselves. W
 e’ll take a historical tour of campus on our way between the museums\, a
 nd we’ll wind up our afternoon with an informal chat at the McCalla Scho
 ol—home to IU’s wonderful University Collections.\nThe structure of th
 is event is unusual (and exciting) for the Traveling University.\nParticip
 ants will meet at the IU Art Museum atrium at 1 pm on Apr. 24 where they w
 ill be greeted by curators and shown the new Mulyana: Vital Ecosystems sho
 w.\nThat visit to the IU Art Museum will be followed by a short historical
  campus tour (c. 2-230 pm) en route to the IU Museum of Archaeology and An
 thropology. Participants will meet with curators before viewing their new 
 Shipwrecks: Living Museums show.\nThe event will finish up (c. 3:30) at th
 e McCalla School where participants will learn more about University Colle
 ctions and spend half hour or so debriefing on the day. Estimated finish: 
 4 or 4:30.\nWe will ask participants to preregister as this event is limit
 ed to 25 participants.\n\n\n\n\nContact\ntravelinguniv@gmail.com
LOCATION:Indiana University Art Museum\, 1133 E 7th St\, Bloomington
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/the-museum-in-question-an-inside-look-at-two-ne
 w-iu-exhibitions/
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//
 EN'>\n<HTML>\n<HEAD>\n<TITLE></TITLE>\n</HEAD>\n<BODY><p data-rte-preserve
 -empty='true'>How do museums differ from classrooms\, publications\, and o
 ther learning media? What do museum people want their visitors to learn an
 d feel—and what preconceptions help or hinder visitors from meeting thos
 e expectations? Eric Sandweiss\, Thomas and Kathryn Miller Professor of Hi
 story\, offers an insider’s look at two exciting new IU exhibitions that
  allows us to hear how museum people think—and to respond for ourselves.
  We’ll take a historical tour of campus on our way between the museums\,
  and we’ll wind up our afternoon with an informal chat at the McCalla Sc
 hool—home to IU’s wonderful University Collections.</p>\n<p class='' d
 ata-rte-preserve-empty='true'>The structure of this event is unusual (and 
 exciting) for the Traveling University.</p>\n<p class='' data-rte-preserve
 -empty='true'>Participants will meet at the IU Art Museum atrium at 1 pm o
 n Apr. 24 where they will be greeted by curators and shown the new <a href
 ='https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/upcoming/_feature-exhibitions/
 2026-02-07-mulyana-vital-ecosystems.html'><em>Mulyana: Vital Ecosystems</e
 m></a> show.</p>\n<p class='' data-rte-preserve-empty='true'>That visit to
  the IU Art Museum will be followed by a short historical campus tour (c. 
 2-230 pm) en route to the IU Museum of Archaeology and Anthropology. Parti
 cipants will meet with curators before viewing their new <a href='https://
 iumaa.iu.edu/exhibits/upcoming-exhibitions/index.html'><em>Shipwrecks: Liv
 ing Museums</em></a> show.</p>\n<p class='' data-rte-preserve-empty='true'
 >The event will finish up (c. 3:30) at the McCalla School where participan
 ts will learn more about University Collections and spend half hour or so 
 debriefing on the day. Estimated finish: 4 or 4:30.</p>\n<p class='' data-
 rte-preserve-empty='true'>We will ask participants to preregister as this 
 event is limited to 25 participants.</p>\n<div class='fe-block fe-block-61
 395d3b53258d7a9c4b'>\n<div id='block-61395d3b53258d7a9c4b' class='sqs-bloc
 k html-block sqs-block-html' data-blend-mode='NORMAL' data-block-type='2' 
 data-border-radii='{'topLeft':{'unit':'px'\,'value':0.0}\,'topRight':{'uni
 t':'px'\,'value':0.0}\,'bottomLeft':{'unit':'px'\,'value':0.0}\,'bottomRig
 ht':{'unit':'px'\,'value':0.0}}' data-sqsp-block='text'>\n<div class='sqs-
 block-content'>\n<div class='sqs-html-content' data-sqsp-text-block-conten
 t=''>\n<h4>Contact</h4>\n<p class=''>travelinguniv@gmail.com</p>\n</div>\n
 </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-COST-TYPE:free
END:VEVENT
