DESCRIPTION:This session offers a focused\, low‑pressure environment whe
 re you can search for scholarships using trusted websites\, ask questions\
 , and start building a list of opportunities to apply for—no application
 s are due during the workshop.During this session\, you will:Use reputable
  scholarship search tools to find current opportunities  Learn strategies 
 for filtering and identifying scholarships you may be eligible for  Save a
 nd organize scholarships to apply for later  Gain a clearer understanding 
 of common scholarship requirements and timelines  Who should attend:  Pre-
 business students and friendsWhat to bring (optional):Resume or list of ac
 tivities\, awards\, and work experience  Basic academic information (major
 \, GPA\, expected graduation year)    Staff will be available throughout t
 he hour to answer questions and help you stay on track. Even if you've nev
 er applied for a scholarship before\, this is a great place to start.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260330T181409Z
LOCATION:Hodge Hall - Room Number: 4083
URL:https://events.iu.edu/kelleyiub/event/2253359-lets-look-together-schol
 arship-search-lab
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This session offers a focused\, low‑pr
 essure environment where you can search for scholarships using trusted web
 sites\, ask questions\, and start building a list of opportunities to appl
 y for—no applications are due during the workshop.</p><p><strong>During 
 this session\, you will:</strong></p><ul><li>Use reputable scholarship sea
 rch tools to find current opportunities  </li><li>Learn strategies for fil
 tering and identifying scholarships you may be eligible for  </li><li>Save
  and organize scholarships to apply for later  </li><li>Gain a clearer und
 erstanding of common scholarship requirements and timelines  </li></ul><p>
 <strong>Who should attend:</strong><br />  Pre-business students and frien
 ds</p><p><strong>What to bring (optional):</strong></p><ul><li>Resume or l
 ist of activities\, awards\, and work experience  </li><li>Basic academic 
 information (major\, GPA\, expected graduation year)  </li></ul><p>  Staff
  will be available throughout the hour to answer questions and help you st
 ay on track. Even if you've never applied for a scholarship before\, this 
 is a great place to start.</p>
