X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2139681-taiwan-studies-initiative-milk-tea-month-the-milk"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_arts_humanities
X-SOURCE:IU Arts & Humanities Institute, IU Asian Culture Center, IU Hamilton Lugar School
SUMMARY:Taiwan Studies Initiative Milk Tea Month: The Milk Tea Alliance
DTSTART:20260424T160000Z
DTEND:20260424T173000Z
DTSTAMP:20260413T103420Z
UID:20260424T160000Z-2266827@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260424T160000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/140/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1545,1999/30736_Jeffrey_Wasserstrom_Flyer_-_CORRECT.rev.1
 774973591.png
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conference
 s
DESCRIPTION:Historian Jeffrey Wasserstrom met dozens of dissidents\, inclu
 ding Netiwit Chotiphatphaisal\, known for his protests against compulsory 
 Thai military service\; Agnes Chow\, co-founder of a political party now b
 anned in Hong Kong\; and Ye Myint Win (aka Nickey Diamond)\, who fled to G
 ermany from Burma in the early 2020s\, fearing reprisal from the junta for
  his human rights work. Activists like these three express solidarity with
  one another online and on the streets\, and sometimes refer to themselves
  as belonging to the "Milk Tea Alliance\," a nod to their shared oppositio
 n to nationalistic Beijing loyalists and the fact that their cultures' ico
 nic drinks contain dairy\, unlike mainland China's traditional tea.  How d
 o these activists\, each facing their unique situations\, find common grou
 nd and sustain one another? Wasserstrom traveled globally to interview mem
 bers of this loosely constituted alliance\, meeting some in Asia and other
 s in exile\, finding them united by democratic values\, shared concerns ov
 er autocrats\, and the rising influence of a common adversary—the Chines
 e Communist Party.  During this talk\, Dr. Wasserstrom will discuss his re
 search and include additional content with a special focus on Taiwan.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260413T143420Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING - Room Number: 2067
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2139681-taiwan-studies-initiative-mi
 lk-tea-month-the-milk
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p class="cvGsUA direction-ltr align-start pa
 ra-style-body">  Historian Jeffrey Wasserstrom met dozens of dissidents\, 
 including Netiwit Chotiphatphaisal\, known for his protests against compul
 sory Thai military service\; Agnes Chow\, co-founder of a political party 
 now banned in Hong Kong\; and Ye Myint Win (aka Nickey Diamond)\, who fled
  to Germany from Burma in the early 2020s\, fearing reprisal from the junt
 a for his human rights work. Activists like these three express solidarity
  with one another online and on the streets\, and sometimes refer to thems
 elves as belonging to the "Milk Tea Alliance\," a nod to their shared oppo
 sition to nationalistic Beijing loyalists and the fact that their cultures
 ' iconic drinks contain dairy\, unlike mainland China's traditional tea.<b
 r /><br />  How do these activists\, each facing their unique situations\,
  find common ground and sustain one another? Wasserstrom traveled globally
  to interview members of this loosely constituted alliance\, meeting some 
 in Asia and others in exile\, finding them united by democratic values\, s
 hared concerns over autocrats\, and the rising influence of a common adver
 sary—the Chinese Communist Party.</p><p class="cvGsUA direction-ltr alig
 n-start para-style-body">  During this talk\, Dr. Wasserstrom will discuss
  his research and include additional content with a special focus on Taiwa
 n.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  taiwansp@iu.edu\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CUSTOM-CUSTOM-RSVP-FIELDS:a:0:{}
X-LIVEWHALE-CUSTOM-ROOM-NUMBER:2067
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2266827
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/140/width/168/heigh
 t/168/crop/1/src_region/0\,0\,1545\,1999/30736_Jeffrey_Wasserstrom_Flyer_-
 _CORRECT.rev.1774973591.png
X-LIVEWHALE-IMAGE-CAPTION:Event flyer
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<p>\n  Dr. Jeffrey Wasserstrom will give a talk based 
 on his book <em>The Milk Tea Alliance: Inside Asia's Struggle Against Auto
 cracy and Beijing.</em>\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
END:VEVENT
