 EN'>\n<HTML>\n<HEAD>\n<TITLE></TITLE>\n</HEAD>\n<BODY><p>Celebrate Arbor D
 ay by planting a native tree! <strong>Sycamore Land Trust</strong>\, a non
 profit conservation organization protecting over 11\,800 acres in southern
  Indiana\, will give away more than 800 free native tree seedlings on Satu
 rday\, April 25\, from 10 a.m. to 2 p.m. at Bloomingfoods East (3220 E. 3r
 d St.) and Bloomingfoods Near West (316 W. 6th St.) in Bloomington. Availa
 ble species include elderberry\, eastern redbud\, persimmon\, gray dogwood
 \, ninebark\, and red oak. This event is sponsored by IU Health and co-hos
 ted by Bloomingfoods Co-op Market. Tree seedlings were grown by the Indian
 a Department of Natural Resources. One free tree seedling per person while
