BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"CitySpark Bloomington": "https://artistsforclimateawareness.org/event/climate-co-lab/", "Limestone Post": "https://artistsforclimateawareness.org/event/climate-co-lab/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"CitySpark Bloomington": "https://artistsforclimateawareness.org/event/climate-co-lab/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:cityspark_bloomington
SUMMARY:"Art as Inquiry\," A Gallery Show
DTSTART;TZID=EDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T120000
DTEND;TZID=EDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260425T180000
UID:260324i4J-ZpztY0eKL1Fggec5bA
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://citysparkstorage.blob.core.windows.net/p
 ortalimages/portalimages/097SR9X5a0SwI2ehnhJKgw.large.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Artists for Climate Awareness invites people of all ages to ex
 perience “Art as Inquiry\,” a juried climate‑art exhibition on view 
 April 2–29 at the Pillar Arts Alliance Center in Bloomington\, IN and on
 line. Featuring 2‑D and 3‑D works from artists across several states\,
  this Earth Month exhibition explores urgent climate and environmental iss
 ues through creative expression and community engagement.\n\nArt\, especia
 lly\, can turn scientific knowledge into experiences that resonate emotion
 ally—offering insights that facts and figures alone can’t always reach
 . When these perspectives come together\, they open up fresh ways of seein
 g and help people connect more deeply with complex ideas. “Art as Inquir
 y” invites visitors to encounter climate research\, ecological change\, 
 and environmental justice through the lens of artistic imagination.\n\nBeg
 inning April 19\, artwork from the Climate Co‑lab \\(Brushes for a Bette
 r Planet\\) joins the exhibition\, displayed alongside the Art as Inquiry 
 works.\n\nEarth Month Events \\(Free\; Public Invited\\):\n\nApril 12\, 2
 –3 pm – Nature Walk\, a musical and narrative performance led by IU Ja
 cobs School of Music student Thejas Mirle and four composers\, with narrat
 ion by Distinguished IU Biology Professor Roger Hangarter.\n\nApril 12\, 3
 –5 pm – Reception for the member climate‑art exhibition\; prizes awa
 rded. 🌱\n\nApril 19\, 3–6 pm – Climate Co‑lab Reception \\+ Natur
 e Walk performance\; brief introductions of artists and partners.\n\nGalle
 ry Hours: • Thu–Sat: 2–8 pm • Sun: 12–6 pm Pillar Arts Alliance 
 Center\, College Mall\, Bloomington. Free admission.
LOCATION:Pillar Arts Alliance Center
URL:https://artistsforclimateawareness.org/event/climate-co-lab/
X-SOURCE:CitySpark Bloomington, Limestone Post
END:VEVENT
