X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2123884-drop-in-tours-and-crafting", "Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2123884-drop-in-tours-and-crafting"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2123884-drop-in-tours-and-crafting"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_arts_humanities
X-SOURCE:Eskenazi Museum of Art, IU Arts & Humanities Institute
SUMMARY:Drop-in Tours and Crafting
DTSTART:20260425T150000Z
DTEND:20260425T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260109T124319Z
UID:20260425T150000Z-2165202@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260425T150000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/29054_Drop-in_Tours__Crafting.rev.1763558113.pn
 g
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:An Immersive ExperienceInspired by Indonesia's spectacular cor
 al reefs\, acclaimed fiber artist Mulyana (b. 1984\, Bandung\, Indonesia) 
 invites you to wander through a handcrafted seascape where art and ecology
  meet.  Explore colorful coral reefs\, playful fish\, and fantastical sea 
 creatures — all meticulously hand-knit and crocheted.  Pause to reflect 
 on the delicate balance between human wellbeing and the vitality of our oc
 eans.  Chat with a Museum Guide to deepen your understanding.  Create Your
  Own Sea CreatureEnjoy a hands-on activity in the gallery.  No prior exper
 ience is needed — a volunteer can guide you step by step.  Choose from a
  fish\, octopus\, lobster\, sea urchin\, or crab.  All supplies are provid
 ed\, so you can dive right in!  Why Visit? This exhibition is more than ar
 t — it's a living conversation about beauty\, fragility\, and our shared
  responsibility to protect the ocean. Whether you're an art lover\, a fami
 ly looking for a creative activity\, or simply curious\, Vital Ecosystems 
 offers a memorable experience for all ages.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260109T174319Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART - Room Number: Featured Ex
 hibitions Gallery\, First Floor
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2123884-drop-in-tours-and-crafting
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h4><strong>An Immersive Experience</strong><
 /h4><ul><li>Inspired by Indonesia's spectacular coral reefs\, acclaimed fi
 ber artist Mulyana (b. 1984\, Bandung\, Indonesia) invites you to wander t
 hrough a handcrafted seascape where art and ecology meet.  </li><li>Explor
 e colorful coral reefs\, playful fish\, and fantastical sea creatures — 
 all meticulously hand-knit and crocheted.  </li><li>Pause to reflect on th
 e delicate balance between human wellbeing and the vitality of our oceans.
   </li><li>Chat with a Museum Guide to deepen your understanding.  </li></
 ul><h4><strong>Create Your Own Sea Creature</strong></h4><ul><li>Enjoy a h
 ands-on activity in the gallery.  </li><li>No prior experience is needed 
 — a volunteer can guide you step by step.  </li><li>Choose from a fish\,
  octopus\, lobster\, sea urchin\, or crab.  </li><li>All supplies are prov
 ided\, so you can dive right in!  </li></ul><p><strong>Why Visit?</strong>
  This exhibition is more than art — it's a living conversation about bea
 uty\, fragility\, and our shared responsibility to protect the ocean. Whet
 her you're an art lover\, a family looking for a creative activity\, or si
 mply curious\, <em>Vital Ecosystems</em> offers a memorable experience for
  all ages.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  ematours@iu.edu\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
