  www.stagesbloomington.org
DESCRIPTION:Once upon a time\, in a far away swamp\, there lived an ogre n
 amed Shrek.  One day\, Shrek finds his swamp invaded by banished fairyta
 le misfits who have been cast off by Lord Farquaad\, a tiny terror with bi
 g ambitions. When Shrek sets off with a wisecracking donkey to confront Fa
 rquaad\, he’s handed a task — if he rescues feisty princess Fiona\, hi
 s swamp will be righted. Shrek tries to win Fiona’s love and vanquish Lo
 rd Farquaad\, but a fairytale wouldn’t be complete without a few twists 
 and turns along the way.\nPart romance and part twisted fairy tale\, Shre
 k JR. is an irreverently fun show with a powerful message for the whole fa
 mily.\nApril 24\, 7:00 pm\nApril 25\, 2:00 pm & 7:00 pm\nApril 26\, noon\n
 Directed by Annalise Cain\nMusic Direction By Ben Handel\nChoreography by 
 Jada Buehler\nStage Management by Kyli Gott-Jacobs\nSet Design by Brian Le
 wis\nCostume Design by Becky Underwood\nProps Design by Leah Tannen\nAssis
 tant Direction by Liz Higgs\nProduction Assistance by Leah Rodkin
LOCATION:The Warehouse Bloomington: 1525 S. Rogers St.
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/shrek-the-musical-jr-3/
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//
 EN'>\n<HTML>\n<HEAD>\n<TITLE></TITLE>\n</HEAD>\n<BODY><p>Once upon a time\
 , in a far away swamp\, there lived an ogre named Shrek.  One day\, Shre
 k finds his swamp invaded by banished fairytale misfits who have been cast
  off by Lord Farquaad\, a tiny terror with big ambitions. When Shrek sets 
 off with a wisecracking donkey to confront Farquaad\, he’s handed a task
  — if he rescues feisty princess Fiona\, his swamp will be righted. Shre
 k tries to win Fiona’s love and vanquish Lord Farquaad\, but a fairytale
  wouldn’t be complete without a few twists and turns along the way.</p>
 \n<p>Part romance and part twisted fairy tale\, Shrek JR. is an irreverent
 ly fun show with a powerful message for the whole family.</p>\n<p>April 24
 \, 7:00 pm<br />\nApril 25\, 2:00 pm & 7:00 pm<br />\nApril 26\, noon</p>\
 n<p>Directed by Annalise Cain<br />\nMusic Direction By Ben Handel<br />\n
 Choreography by Jada Buehler<br />\nStage Management by Kyli Gott-Jacobs<b
 r />\nSet Design by Brian Lewis<br />\nCostume Design by Becky Underwood<b
 r />\nProps Design by Leah Tannen<br />\nAssistant Direction by Liz Higgs<
 br />\nProduction Assistance by Leah Rodkin</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
