SUMMARY:Frog Songs
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260426T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260426T200000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020748Z
UID:1bkon2u1ja0gv6ugnlkhgdp9e8@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260426T183000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20251205T171724Z
DESCRIPTION:Registration fee $/in-city\, $6/non-city. Register online by A
 pril 22 at <a href="https://webtrac.bloomington.in.gov/webtrac/web/search
 .html?Primarycode=140005">https://webtrac.bloomington.in.gov/webtrac/web/s
 earch.html?Primarycode=140005</a><br>For all ages.<br>Frogs make a variety
  of noises\, from croaks to peeps. These distinctive calls help them attra
 ct mates\, protect themselves\, and even alert others of danger. Join us f
 or a hike around Griffy Lake to learn about the interesting sounds frogs m
 ake\, and see them in action. Participants should wear shoes that can get 
 muddy and be able to hike on moderate terrain.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251205T171724Z
LOCATION:Griffy Lake Nature Preserve\, 3400 N Headley Rd\, Bloomington\, I
 N 47408\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
