ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/135/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1280,720/30894_Indiana_University_Bloomington_-_India_Cor
 ner.rev.1776096973.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages,Functions, fes
 tivals, and celebrations,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences
DESCRIPTION:Deepen your perspective. Access the collection. Meet a veteran
  practitioner.  The Hamilton Lugar School is officially opening the India 
 Corner\, a new specialized lending library and resource hub. This curated 
 collection offers a deep dive into Indian cultural history\, regional lite
 rature\, and social perspectives—providing the essential context needed 
 to understand one of the world's most significant global powers.  To mark 
 the inauguration of this collection\, join us for a briefing with Consul G
 eneral Somnath Ghosh on the intersection of culture\, history\, and modern
  diplomacy.The Main Event: Ambassador Somnath GhoshAmbassador Ghosh (https
 ://www.cgichicago.gov.in/page/profile/) brings 28 years of diplomatic trad
 ecraft to GISB. Before his current assignment in Chicago\, he led Internat
 ional Cooperation in India's Ministry of Defence\, managing complex policy
  and negotiations with the U.S.\, Russia\, and the UK. He offers a unique 
 look at how a deep understanding of history and regional identity informs 
 high-stakes global security and the Indo-Pacific strategy.  Refreshments p
 rovided. Hamilton Lugar School's Office of Policy Engagement and Strategic
  Partnerships and Dhar India Studies&#160\;
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T134612Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING - Room Number: 4067
URL:https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2267016-the-india-corner-collection-la
 unch-and-remarks-by
