 s
DESCRIPTION:The Center for Latin American and Caribbean Studies is proud t
 o present the continuation of its Colloquium Series for Spring 2026.  We w
 elcome Dr. Lucia Guerra Reyes&#160\;as she presents Circulating Latin Amer
 ica: Ethical Interventions from the Global South.Lucia Guerra-Reyes is an 
 associate professor in applied health science. She is a medical anthropolo
 gist and interdisciplinary researcher. Guerra-Reyes investigates the compl
 exities of access to sexual and reproductive health and care for marginali
 zed communities. She is interested in understanding how national policies 
 of culturally appropriate care are enacted at the local level\; how health
  care providers view their role in extending care to under-served communit
 ies\; and how women make decisions about their reproductive lives.&#160\; 
  &#160\;  The CLACS Spring 2026 Colloquium meets Mondays from February thr
 ough April\, with faculty and guest speakers engaging Latin America and th
 e Caribbean through research on history\, culture\, language\, politics\, 
 and the arts. Check the CLACS Calendar (https://events.iu.edu/clacs/) for 
 details.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260415T200613Z
LOCATION:355 N. Eagleson Avenue - Room Number: 1060
