END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Hamilton Lugar School": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2190070-workshop-on-measuring-international-development"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_hamilton_lugar
X-SOURCE:IU Hamilton Lugar School
SUMMARY:Workshop on Measuring International Development\, Advancing Equity
DTSTART:20260428T120000Z
DTEND:20260428T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260213T130019Z
UID:20260428T120000Z-2209431@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260428T120000Z
CATEGORIES:Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,Performances, shows,
  and films,Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Humanity stands at a crossroads. While we have made incredible
  strides in human development\, we also face existential threats—from cl
 imate change and pandemics to growing polarization and inequality. To over
 come these threats\, we must work together to advance a coherent vision of
  human development centered on guaranteeing every person a dignified\, or 
 at least minimally good\, life. This workshop addresses the conceptual and
  practical gaps in how we measure social progress. A narrow focus on GDP i
 s no longer sufficient\; it is distribution-insensitive and fails to captu
 re the non-market values essential for mutual flourishing. This workshop w
 ill explore how to think about development\, develop better metrics\, and 
 put them into practice.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260216T192339Z
LOCATION:GISB - Room Number: 1060
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2190070-workshop-on-measuring-intern
 ational-development
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Humanity stands at a crossroads. While w
 e have made incredible strides in human development\, we also face existen
 tial threats—from climate change and pandemics to growing polarization a
 nd inequality. To overcome these threats\, we must work together to advanc
 e a coherent vision of human development centered on guaranteeing every pe
 rson a dignified\, or at least minimally good\, life. This workshop addres
 ses the conceptual and practical gaps in how we measure social progress. A
  narrow focus on GDP is no longer sufficient\; it is distribution-insensit
 ive and fails to capture the non-market values essential for mutual flouri
 shing. This workshop will explore how to think about development\, develop
  better metrics\, and put them into practice.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CUSTOM-ROOM-NUMBER:1060
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:2209431
X-LIVEWHALE-RSVP:1
X-LIVEWHALE-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
X-LIVEWHALE-TYPE:events
END:VEVENT
