BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/death-cafe-8/?instance_id=94732"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/death-cafe-8/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:wfhb
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
SUMMARY:Death Cafe
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T200000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020832Z
UID:ai1ec-148032@wfhb.org
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T190000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:A Death Cafe is a group-directed discussion of death with no a
 genda\, ideology\, objectives\, or themes. It is a discussion group rather
  than grief support or counseling session. Death Cafes have spread quickly
  around the world. Over 16\,500 Death Cafes are held in 85 countries. All 
 are volunteer-run.\nThe monthly Death Cafe at Morgenstern Books is run by 
 co-hosts Rick Clayton and Casey Stover. Rick Clayton is a hospice chaplain
 \, end-of life doula\, and musician who enjoys playing harp\, cello\, and 
 guitar for his clients. Casey Stover is a Certified Family Life Educator w
 hose professional work often exists adjacent to death and grief\, shaping 
 her belief in the importance of accessible spaces to normalize honest conv
 ersation and community care.\nYou can find our Death Cafe at the back corn
 er of the bookstore\, near the restrooms\, on the last Tuesday of every mo
 nth at 7 pm.
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/death-cafe-8/
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//
 EN'>\n<HTML>\n<HEAD>\n<TITLE></TITLE>\n</HEAD>\n<BODY><p dir='ltr'>A Death
  Cafe is a group-directed discussion of death with no agenda\, ideology\, 
 objectives\, or themes. It is a discussion group rather than grief support
  or counseling session. Death Cafes have spread quickly around the world. 
 Over 16\,500 Death Cafes are held in 85 countries. All are volunteer-run.<
 /p>\n<p dir='ltr'>The monthly Death Cafe at Morgenstern Books is run by co
 -hosts Rick Clayton and Casey Stover. Rick Clayton is a hospice chaplain\,
  end-of life doula\, and musician who enjoys playing harp\, cello\, and gu
 itar for his clients. Casey Stover is a Certified Family Life Educator who
 se professional work often exists adjacent to death and grief\, shaping he
 r belief in the importance of accessible spaces to normalize honest conver
 sation and community care.</p>\n<p dir='ltr'>You can find our Death Cafe a
 t the back corner of the bookstore\, near the restrooms\, on the last Tues
 day of every month at 7 pm.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-COST-TYPE:free
END:VEVENT
