X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Black Film Center & Archive": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2246096-when-everyone-swims-w-qampa-new-americas-cinema", "IU Cinema": "https://events.iu.edu/cinemaiub/event/2246096-when-everyone-swims-wfilmmaker-new-americas-cinema", "Bloomington Arts": "https://tockify.com/bloomington.arts.calendar/detail/2093/1777417200000"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Black Film Center & Archive": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2246096-when-everyone-swims-w-qampa-new-americas-cinema"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_black_film
X-SOURCE:IU Black Film Center & Archive, IU Cinema, Bloomington Arts
SUMMARY:When Everyone Swims w/filmmaker | New Americas Cinema
DTSTART:20260428T230000Z
DTEND:20260429T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260323T155010Z
UID:20260428T230000Z-2246116@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260428T230000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/81/width/168/height/168/crop/1
 /src_region/0,0,1920,1080/30603_When_Everyone_Swims_1920x1080.rev.17742938
 90.png
CATEGORIES:Culture and languages,Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:When Everyone Swims is a compilation of inspirational and insi
 ghtful stories about how everyone deserves access to pools and safe places
  to swim. Through powerful\, personal narratives\, the film celebrates res
 ilience and highlights how water literacy can help individuals from all ba
 ckgrounds build healthy\, life-affirming relationships with the water. [90
  min\; documentary\; English]A Q&amp\;A with director Jerald Harkness\, Ol
 ympic medalist Lilly King\, and production consultant Dr. Tiffany Monique 
 Quash\, moderated by Bill Ramos of the School of Public Health\, will foll
 ow the screening.
GEO:39.168613;-86.517376
LAST-MODIFIED:20260324T192952Z
LOCATION:IU CINEMA
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2246096-when-everyone-swims-w-qampa-
 new-americas-cinema
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><i>When Everyone Swims</i> is a compilatio
 n of inspirational and insightful stories about how everyone deserves acce
 ss to pools and safe places to swim. Through powerful\, personal narrative
 s\, the film celebrates resilience and highlights how water literacy can h
 elp individuals from all backgrounds build healthy\, life-affirming relati
 onships with the water. [90 min\; documentary\; English]</p><p><i><strong>
 A Q&amp\;A with director Jerald Harkness\, Olympic medalist Lilly King\, a
 nd production consultant Dr. Tiffany Monique Quash\, moderated by Bill Ram
 os of the School of Public Health\, will follow the screening.</strong></i
 ></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  <a href="mailto:iucinema@iu.edu">iucinema@
 iu.edu</a> // 812-856-CINE\n</p>
