CATEGORIES:Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Dive deep into the archival collections of IU Libraries Moving
  Image Archive through a new monthly screening series of short films! Each
  month\, rare and unique archival films will be presented focusing on unde
 rrepresented narratives and underrepresented motion-picture practices that
  push on and expand the spectrum of what is considered "cinema."  In an ef
 fort to keep audiences open-minded and with limited pre-conceptions of the
 se rare works of celluloid\, descriptions of films to be shown will not be
  shared prior to screenings. Join us based on announced themes and the exp
 ectation that the works you see will fall outside of Hollywood tropes\, ou
 tside of mainstream commercial expectations\, and outside of conventional 
 filmmaking practices. Trust us\, you (probably) haven't seen these films b
 efore!  This program is curated by Dominick Rivers and hosted by the IU Li
 braries Moving Image Archive Screening Room.  Please remember to register 
 below.
GEO:39.171006;-86.5168
LAST-MODIFIED:20260417T151438Z
LOCATION:Wells Library Screening Room 048
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2169132-you-probably-havent-seen
 -this-before
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Dive deep into the archival collections 
 of IU Libraries Moving Image Archive through a new monthly screening serie
 s of short films! Each month\, rare and unique archival films will be pres
 ented focusing on underrepresented narratives and underrepresented motion-
 picture practices that push on and expand the spectrum of what is consider
 ed "cinema."</p><p>  In an effort to keep audiences open-minded and with l
 imited pre-conceptions of these rare works of celluloid\, descriptions of 
 films to be shown will not be shared prior to screenings. Join us based on
  announced themes and the expectation that the works you see will fall out
 side of Hollywood tropes\, outside of mainstream commercial expectations\,
  and outside of conventional filmmaking practices. Trust us\, you (probabl
 y) haven't seen these films before!</p><p>  This program is curated by <sp
 an data-olk-copy-source="MailCompose">Dominick Rivers</span> and hosted by
  the IU Libraries Moving Image Archive Screening Room.</p><p>  Please reme
 mber to register below.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
