SUMMARY:By Their Own Hands: The Black Filmmakers Hall of Fame exhibit
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260502
DTSTAMP:20251015T135318Z
UID:20260501T040000Z-2087617@events.iu.edu__20260501
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/221/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,881,604/28658_BFHF.rev.1760550782.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages,Functions, fes
 tivals, and celebrations,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,Perfor
 mances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:By Their Own Hands includes one-of-a-kind items such as Sidney
  Poitier's autographed shooting script for Let's Do It Again (1975)\, the 
 Nicholas Brothers' tap shoes\, and letters from icons like Maya Angelou an
 d Oprah Winfrey\, among others. The centerpiece is a stunning wall of 42 B
 FHFI inductees' handprints\, a distinction comparable to receiving a star 
 on the Hollywood Walk of Fame! Select examples of inductees' handprints in
 clude Lena Horne\, Eartha Kitt\, Richard Pryor\, and Billy Dee Williams.  
 Special thanks to University Collections at McCalla for collaborating with
  and helping install the exhibit\, and to the IU Foundation's Affinity Giv
 ing Group – Black Philanthropy Circle (BPC) for generously awarding the 
 BFCA a grant to frame the handprints in Summer 2024.By Their Own Hands wil
 l remain on display through Spring 2026\, and the BFCA will hold an educat
 ional event to re-engage the exhibit space during Black History Month. Con
 tact us at bfca@iu.edu to request an appointment to view BFHFI collection 
 items not curated for the exhibit.
GEO:39.170841;-86.5275
LAST-MODIFIED:20251015T175318Z
LOCATION:MCCALLA
URL:https://events.iu.edu/bfca/event/2087617-by-their-own-hands-the-black-
 filmmakers-hall-of
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><em data-olk-copy-source="MessageBody">By 
 Their Own Hands</em> includes one-of-a-kind items such as Sidney Poitier's
  autographed shooting script for <em>Let's Do It Again</em> (1975)\, the N
 icholas Brothers' tap shoes\, and letters from icons like Maya Angelou and
  Oprah Winfrey\, among others. The centerpiece is a stunning wall of 42 BF
 HFI inductees' handprints\, a distinction comparable to receiving a star o
 n the Hollywood Walk of Fame! Select examples of inductees' handprints inc
 lude Lena Horne\, Eartha Kitt\, Richard Pryor\, and Billy Dee Williams.</p
 ><p>  Special thanks to University Collections at McCalla for collaboratin
 g with and helping install the exhibit\, and to the IU Foundation's Affini
 ty Giving Group – Black Philanthropy Circle (BPC) for generously awardin
 g the BFCA a grant to frame the handprints in Summer 2024.</p><p><em>By Th
 eir Own Hands</em> will remain on display through Spring 2026\, and the BF
 CA will hold an educational event to re-engage the exhibit space during Bl
 ack History Month. Contact us at bfca@iu.edu to request an appointment to 
 view BFHFI collection items not curated for the exhibit.</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ALL-DAY:1
