CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Culture and languages,Functions, fes
 tivals, and celebrations,Performances, shows, and films
DESCRIPTION:Donated by the Vieyra family in June 2021\, the exhibition sho
 wcases highlights from The Paulin S. Vieyra Collection. The display case f
 eatures intimate and rare items\, including family portraits\, Vieyra's ty
 pewriter\, and a 16mm reel of Môl (1966). Five original collages by graph
 ic designer Pouya Jahanshahi are at the center of the exhibition. Jahansha
 hi collaborated with Project Archivist Jason Byrne\, who shaped the exhibi
 tion's themes and selected archival content. Student workers Sarah Petras\
 , Thomas Pigott\, Cree Prince\, and Kudzai Zinyemba supported the project 
 by helping process and research the materials.  The TOTAL AFRICAN CINEMA e
 xhibit is on view in the BFCA reception area now through May 31\, 2026!
GEO:39.171255;-86.516556
LAST-MODIFIED:20250801T162531Z
LOCATION:Black Film Center and Archive\, 1320 E. 10th Street\, Wells Libra
 ry 044\, Bloomington\, IN\, 47405 - Room Number: Exhibit/Reception Area
URL:https://events.iu.edu/bfca/event/2005251-total-african-cinema-exhibit
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Donated by the Vieyra family in June 202
 1\, the exhibition showcases highlights from The Paulin S. Vieyra Collecti
 on. The display case features intimate and rare items\, including family p
 ortraits\, Vieyra's typewriter\, and a 16mm reel of <em>Môl</em> (1966). 
 Five original collages by graphic designer Pouya Jahanshahi are at the cen
 ter of the exhibition. Jahanshahi collaborated with Project Archivist Jaso
 n Byrne\, who shaped the exhibition's themes and selected archival content
 . Student workers Sarah Petras\, Thomas Pigott\, Cree Prince\, and Kudzai 
 Zinyemba supported the project by helping process and research the materia
 ls.</p><p>  The <em>TOTAL AFRICAN CINEMA</em> exhibit is on view in the BF
 CA reception area now through May 31\, 2026!</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ALL-DAY:1
