DESCRIPTION:May 1\, 2026\, 9:00 AM - 12:30 PMFerguson International Center
 \, 4th FloorPoster Set-up: 8:45–9:20 AM  Light Breakfast: 9:00–9:30 AM
   Keynote Address: 9:30–10:45 AM  Poster Session: 11:00 AM – 12:30 PM 
  Join us for the IU Global Learning Showcase\, a celebration of student an
 d faculty innovation in globally engaged education.  This year's keynote a
 ddress\, "Reimagining Strategies Toward Sub-Saharan Africa: Opportunities 
 for U.S. Cities\, Communities\, and Universities\," will be delivered by J
 udd Devermont\, former National Security Council Senior Director for Afric
 an Affairs and National Intelligence Officer for Africa. He will share les
 sons learned from drafting the Biden Administration's strategy toward the 
 region and discuss opportunities for Indiana's institutions\, leaders\, an
 d citizens to model a new\, more mutually advantageous partnership.  After
  the keynote\, explore a poster sessionfeaturing presentations from global
  client projects\, Collaborative Online International Learning (COIL)\, Di
 plomacy Lab\, and more. Topics span disciplines and highlight how IU stude
 nts and faculty are turning learning into action on today's most pressing 
 global challenges.All are welcome—come be inspired and join us in shapin
 g a more connected world!Present Your Work at the Poster SessionAre you an
  IU student or instructor engaged in global learning? We invite you to sha
 re your work during the poster session. This is a great opportunity to sho
 wcase project-based or experiential learning projects\, connect with other
 s\, and highlight how global learning is happening here in Indiana and bey
 ond.  Poster printing costs will be covered. View poster design and printi
 ng instructions (https://indiana-my.sharepoint.com/:b:/g/personal/amsmithr
 _iu_edu/IQBrbJvE4oUgS4PgcQg6UM9vAdwOWrTxFw2errchiwgnu34?e=QJzdde.).Sign up
