SUMMARY:Strategic Thinking in U.S.-Africa Policy and Intelligence (w/ LUNC
 H)
DTSTART:20260501T153000Z
DTEND:20260501T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20260217T092312Z
UID:20260501T153000Z-2212903@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260501T153000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/135/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,400,400/22976_globalcompetencies.rev.1725026179.jpg
CATEGORIES:Career development,Lectures, talks, seminars, and conferences,T
 raining, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Event Description:  How do policymakers and intelligence offic
 ers navigate complex decisions in Africa and beyond?  Join Judd Devermont 
 (https://www.csis.org/people/judd-devermont)\, former National Intelligenc
 e Officer for Africa and former Senior Director for African Affairs at the
  White House\, for a live\, scenario-driven session on strategy\, risk\, a
 nd global policymaking.  Devermont spent over a decade in the intelligence
  community\, advised two administrations\, authored the U.S. Strategy towa
 rd Sub-Saharan Africa\, and directed major initiatives shaping billions in
  infrastructure\, digital connectivity\, and energy investments.This is no
 t a lecture. You will work through a real-world scenario: African states b
 alancing relationships with the U.S. and China while managing domestic pol
 itical and development pressures.  You'll assess risk\, identify second- a
 nd third-order effects\, evaluate trade-offs\, and recommend a course of a
 ction.What you'll gain:      Insight into how intelligence and policy inte
 rsect          Frameworks to anticipate unintended consequences          H
 ow analysis translates into real-world decisions          A window into ca
 reers in intelligence\, government\, and think tanks    Lunch will be prov
 ided!&#160\;Come ready to debate\, analyze\, and defend your conclusions i
 n an interactive\, off-the-record setting.
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
LAST-MODIFIED:20260324T145206Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING - Room Number: 1118
URL:https://events.iu.edu/hls/event/2212903-strategic-thinking-in-us-afric
 a-policy-and-intellige
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p data-start="144" data-end="168"><strong da
 ta-start="144" data-end="166">Event Description:</strong></p><p data-start
 ="170" data-end="266">  How do policymakers and intelligence officers navi
 gate complex decisions in Africa and beyond?</p><p data-start="268" data-e
 nd="485">  Join <a href="https://www.csis.org/people/judd-devermont">Judd 
 Devermont</a>\, former National Intelligence Officer for Africa and former
  Senior Director for African Affairs at the White House\, for a live\, sce
 nario-driven session on strategy\, risk\, and global policymaking.</p><p d
 ata-start="268" data-end="485"><img src="https://lawfare-assets-new.azuree
 dge.net/assets/images/default-source/contributor-images/3902.jpg?sfvrsn=cb
 a0bcf9_0" alt="" loading="lazy"/></p><p data-start="487" data-end="745">  
 Devermont spent over a decade in the intelligence community\, advised two 
 administrations\, authored the U.S. Strategy toward Sub-Saharan Africa\, a
 nd directed major initiatives shaping billions in infrastructure\, digital
  connectivity\, and energy investments.</p><p data-start="747" data-end="7
 71"><strong>This is not a lecture. You will work through a real-world scen
 ario:</strong> African states balancing relationships with the U.S. and Ch
 ina while managing domestic political and development pressures.</p><p dat
 a-start="945" data-end="1063">  You'll assess risk\, identify second- and 
 third-order effects\, evaluate trade-offs\, and recommend a course of acti
 on.</p><p data-start="1065" data-end="1088"><strong data-start="1065" data
 -end="1086">What you'll gain:</strong></p><ul data-start="1089" data-end="
 1321"><li data-start="1089" data-end="1143"><p data-start="1091" data-end=
 "1143">      Insight into how intelligence and policy intersect    </p></l
 i><li data-start="1144" data-end="1196"><p data-start="1146" data-end="119
 6">      Frameworks to anticipate unintended consequences    </p></li><li 
 data-start="1197" data-end="1250"><p data-start="1199" data-end="1250">   
    How analysis translates into real-world decisions    </p></li><li data-
 start="1251" data-end="1321"><p data-start="1253" data-end="1321">      A 
 window into careers in intelligence\, government\, and think tanks    </p>
 </li></ul><p data-start="1323" data-end="1450"><strong>Lunch will be provi
 ded!</strong>&#160\;Come ready to debate\, analyze\, and defend your concl
 usions in an interactive\, off-the-record setting.</p>
