ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,250,83/29086_Benton_Murals_at_IU_Auditorium.rev.176373147
 0.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:This tour visitsThe Hall of Murals at IU Auditorium  IU Cinema
   Woodburn Hall  About the Indiana Murals:  Thomas Hart Benton was commiss
 ioned to paint murals depicting Indiana history for the Indiana state pavi
 lion at the 1933 World's Fair in Chicago. The dramatic 250-foot long mural
 \, which originally wrapped around the entire exhibition hall at the World
 's Fair\, depicts the social\, economic\, and cultural history of Indiana 
 from mound building to the 1930s. After several years of storage following
  the fair\, the panels were given to Indiana University in 1938\, where th
 ey were installed in three locations on the Bloomington campus.&#160\;Abou
 t Your Guide:  Jim Davis is a Senior Lecturer in the Kelley School of Busi
 ness\, in the department of Management and Entrepreneurship. He has been s
 erving as a docent and museum guide at the IU Eskenazi Museum of Art for t
 he past ten years.&#160\; &#160\; &#160\;Know Before You GoThis tour visit
 s three locations on campus. Please let us know if an elevator and wheelch
 air accessible route will be needed.&#160\;  Plan to arrive at least 5 min
 utes beforehand to check in.For a discounted parking rate for the Indiana 
 Memorial Union parking lot\, visit the Eskenazi Museum of Art before or af
 ter this tour and ask Guest Services\, at the Information Desk on the firs
 t floor\, to stamp your parking voucher.
GEO:39.168443;-86.517858
LAST-MODIFIED:20260210T154959Z
LOCATION:AUDITORIUM - Room Number: Hall of Murals
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2119226-tour-of-thomas-hart-bentons-
 indiana-murals
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This tour visits</p><ul><li>The Hall of 
 Murals at IU Auditorium  </li><li>IU Cinema  </li><li>Woodburn Hall  </li>
 </ul><h4><strong>About the Indiana Murals:</strong></h4><p>  Thomas Hart B
 enton was commissioned to paint murals depicting Indiana history for the I
 ndiana state pavilion at the 1933 World's Fair in Chicago. The dramatic 25
 0-foot long mural\, which originally wrapped around the entire exhibition 
 hall at the World's Fair\, depicts the social\, economic\, and cultural hi
 story of Indiana from mound building to the 1930s. After several years of 
 storage following the fair\, the panels were given to Indiana University i
 n 1938\, where they were installed in three locations on the Bloomington c
 ampus.&#160\;</p><h4><strong>About Your Guide:</strong></h4><p>  Jim Davis
  is a Senior Lecturer in the Kelley School of Business\, in the department
  of Management and Entrepreneurship. He has been serving as a docent and m
 useum guide at the IU Eskenazi Museum of Art for the past ten years.&#160\
