X-SOURCE-URLS:{"CitySpark Bloomington": "https://www.playpensports.com/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:cityspark_bloomington
SUMMARY:Toddler Sports Classes
DTSTART;TZID=EDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T090000
DTEND;TZID=EDT;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T120000
UID:260324AIf4f_fqY0Wpa1M6m2E-xQ
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://citysparkstorage.blob.core.windows.net/p
 ortalimages/portalimages/wWprhzPqOE6BC9X6I0f2DA.large.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Playpen Sports Academy is a wonderful way to introduce your ch
 ild to the world of sport and physical activity in a non-intimidating envi
 ronment with a small group of other toddlers and parents. The Playpen Spor
 ts Academy Curriculum is focused on a number of different goals including 
 teaching children how to move and use their bodies\, sharing with other ch
 ildren\, interact in social settings\, follow directions\, and most import
 antly how to have fun in a physically active environment. At Playpen Sport
 s Academy\, we are focused as much on the individual development of your c
 hild as we are on sport specific skills that we teach. Because while we ex
 pect some of your children to go on to be great athletes\, we expect all o
 f your children to go on to be great people!
URL:https://www.playpensports.com/
X-SOURCE:CitySpark Bloomington
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU beINvolved Student Orgs": "https://iub.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12327214"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_campuslabs
SUMMARY:Graduate Student Conference
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260502T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260502T153000
UID:https://iub.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12327214
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/66
 e2a2e0-556a-4b61-8c59-6cd7bee7a4984aee9afa-4ae7-4130-af02-d36ed8dc29e1.png
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by: Student Advisory Board of the Department of Compara
 tive Literature\n\nIt&rsquo\;s About Time! &nbsp\;--&nbsp\;It is always ti
 mely to talk about time\, but\, perhaps now more than ever\, time is of th
 e essence. So\, what are we waiting for? The central theme of this confere
 nce is temporality &ndash\; which may be broadly defined as the study of t
 ime and experiences related to time. This includes individual and collecti
 ve perceptions of the flow of time\; human and/or non-human experiences of
  time\; changes\, or perceived changes in the flow of time and their effec
 ts on the pace and movement of life\, work\, and art.
LOCATION:IMU Maple Room
URL:https://iub.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12327214
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
END:VEVENT
