BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2158649-writing-in-the-galleries", "Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2158649-writing-in-the-galleries"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2158649-writing-in-the-galleries"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_arts_humanities
X-SOURCE:Eskenazi Museum of Art, IU Arts & Humanities Institute
SUMMARY:Writing in the Galleries
DTSTART:20260502T170000Z
DTEND:20260502T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260109T115743Z
UID:20260502T170000Z-2165158@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260502T170000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/29305_Writing_in_the_Galleries_-_thumbnail.rev.
 1767371047.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, we begin by looking closely at artwork—as
 king what we see\, think\, feel\, and wonder. Together\, we'll explore the
  artist's possible message and its social meaning\, then turn those reflec
 tions into our own creative responses.  Whether you're a writer or simply 
 curious to try something new\, you'll find inspiration here and a welcomin
 g community to share the journey.  What to Bringyour favorite pencil (no p
 ens).  a notebook or paper. Clipboards are available to borrow.  a phone o
 r camera to take a picture of the art for later reference.  Know Before Yo
 u GoArrive early\, check in\, and get ready for an on-time start.Readwhere
  to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.About 
 Your Facilitator  Dedaimia Whitney earned an MFA in fiction from Indiana U
 niversity under the direction of Scott Russell Sanders. She taught creativ
 e writing at Franklin College for many years. She has served the museum as
  a docent since 2019. Her favorite works of art are those that are both vi
 sually stimulating and thought-provoking.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260109T165743Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART - Room Number: Check in on
  the first floor
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2158649-writing-in-the-galleries
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In this workshop\, we begin by looking c
 losely at artwork—asking what we see\, think\, feel\, and wonder. Togeth
 er\, we'll explore the artist's possible message and its social meaning\, 
 then turn those reflections into our own creative responses.</p><p>  Wheth
 er you're a writer or simply curious to try something new\, you'll find in
 spiration here and a welcoming community to share the journey.</p><h3>  Wh
 at to Bring</h3><ul><li>your favorite pencil (no pens).  </li><li>a notebo
 ok or paper. Clipboards are available to borrow.  </li><li>a phone or came
 ra to take a picture of the art for later reference.  </li></ul><h3><stron
 g><span data-contrast="none">Know Before You Go</span></strong></h3><ul><l
 i data-leveltext="" data-font="Symbol" data-listid="2" data-list-defn-p
 rops="{&quot\;335552541&quot\;:1\,&quot\;335559683&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335559
 684&quot\;:-2\,&quot\;335559685&quot\;:720\,&quot\;335559991&quot\;:360\,&
 quot\;469769226&quot\;:&quot\;Symbol&quot\;\,&quot\;469769242&quot\;:[8226
 ]\,&quot\;469777803&quot\;:&quot\;left&quot\;\,&quot\;469777804&quot\;:&qu
 ot\;&quot\;\,&quot\;469777815&quot\;:&quot\;hybridMultilevel&quot\;}" a
