CATEGORIES:Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:During this workshop\, attendees will learn about the Sculptur
 e Trails Outdoor Museum\, see examples of lost-wax and relief sculptures i
 n the Eskenazi Museum of Art's collection\, and will be walked through how
  to carve a relief sculpture on a provided "scratch block." Leading the ca
 rving workshop are Sculpture Trails Outdoor Museum staff Laura Gonzalez (O
 utreach Coordinator) and Ethan Harmon (Artist-in-Residence)\, as well as E
 skenazi Museum of Art's resident Arts-based Wellness Experiences Manager\,
  Keaton Evans-Black.PLEASE NOTE: Your scratch block will be taken to the S
 culpture Trails Outdoor Museum to be completed through their metal pour pr
 ocess. During the workshop\, you must schedule to retrieve your artwork fr
 om either the Eskenazi Museum of Art or the Sculpture Trails Outdoor Museu
 m at a later date.For more information about the Sculpture Trails Outdoor 
 Museum\, click here. (https://sculpturetrails.com/about/)
