X-SOURCE-ID:wfhb
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
SUMMARY:Southern Indiana Wind Ensemble Spring Concert
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T190000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020832Z
UID:ai1ec-147309@wfhb.org
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T190000
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:
CONTACT:
DESCRIPTION:Conductor: Stephen W. Pratt\nThis concert features music that 
 celebrates American music in many ways.\nThe Symphonic Concert March is by
  an Italian composer\, but was rescued from obscurity by Nicholas Falcone\
 , one of two Italian brothers who came to America as teenagers and made a 
 huge impact on the American concert band world in many ways. The Alfred Re
 ed Ballade features our guest soloist\, Dr. Thomas Walsh\, from the Jacobs
  School of Music faculty\, an outstanding saxophonist. Florence Price’s 
 Adoration\, a transcription of her organ piece\, is a beautiful addition t
 o our repertoire. David Dzubay\, from the Jacobs School of Music faculty i
 s represented with his Gloriana\, Frangipana\, a piece he composed. Three 
 iconic American composers are also represented – Bernstein\, Copland\, a
 nd Gershwin. My hope is that every member of the audience will find at lea
 st several pieces that they want to hear and will enjoy.
LOCATION:Bloomington High School North Auditorium\, 3901 N Kinser Pike\, B
 loomington
URL:https://wfhb.org/event/southern-indiana-wind-ensemble-spring-concert-2
 /
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC '-//W3C//DTD HTML 3.2//
 EN'>\n<HTML>\n<HEAD>\n<TITLE></TITLE>\n</HEAD>\n<BODY><p>Conductor: Stephe
 n W. Pratt</p>\n<p>This concert features music that celebrates American mu
 sic in many ways.</p>\n<p>The Symphonic Concert March is by an Italian com
 poser\, but was rescued from obscurity by Nicholas Falcone\, one of two It
 alian brothers who came to America as teenagers and made a huge impact on 
 the American concert band world in many ways. The Alfred Reed Ballade feat
 ures our guest soloist\, Dr. Thomas Walsh\, from the Jacobs School of Musi
 c faculty\, an outstanding saxophonist. Florence Price’s Adoration\, a t
 ranscription of her organ piece\, is a beautiful addition to our repertoir
 e. David Dzubay\, from the Jacobs School of Music faculty is represented w
 ith his Gloriana\, Frangipana\, a piece he composed. Three iconic American
  composers are also represented – Bernstein\, Copland\, and Gershwin. My
  hope is that every member of the audience will find at least several piec
 es that they want to hear and will enjoy.</p>\n</BODY></HTML>
X-COST-TYPE:free
X-INSTANT-EVENT:1
END:VEVENT
