BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Parks And Rec": "https://bloomington.in.gov/farmers-marketThe", "WFHB Community Calendar": "https://wfhb.org/event/bloomington-community-farmers-market-10/?instance_id=94597"}
X-SOURCE-ID:farmers_market
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Community Farmers' Market, Parks And Rec, WFHB Community Calendar
SUMMARY:Bloomington Community Farmers' Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260509T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260509T123000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020750Z
UID:3esrjhm03ndm8a1qu2n1923uv5@google.com__20260509
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20251223T163716Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>The <a href="https://bloomington.in.gov/farmers-market">Blo
 omington Community Farmers' Market</a> takes place rain or shine every Sat
 urday\, April through October\, at <a href="https://bloomington.in.gov/ci
 ty/showers-city-hall"><u>Showers Common next to City Hall</u></a>\, 401 N.
  Morton St. in Bloomington.</p><p>April-September: 8 a.m.-12:30 p.m.<br>Oc
 tober: 9 a.m.-12:30 p.m.<br>November: 9 a.m.-12:30 p.m. at the Pavilion at
  <a href="https://switchyardpark.com/"><u>Switchyard Park</u></a></p><p>T
 he Market is a gathering place where local farmers\, makers\, and neighbor
 s come together to share the foods\, traditions\, and connections that str
 engthen our community and support a reliable local food supply.</p><p>Mark
 et goers find a wide assortment of goods from the farm and field\, includi
 ng fruits and vegetables\, eggs\, meats and cheeses\, honey\, seasonal flo
 wers\, and annual and perennial plants. Food and beverage artisans provide
  a tasteful variety of drinks\, pastries\, and savory dishes. This weekly 
 gathering provides opportunities for individuals to connect with their com
 munity in meaningful ways and support local farmers and small businesses.<
 /p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251223T163734Z
LOCATION:City of Bloomington\, 401 N Morton St\, Bloomington\, IN 47404\, 
 USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU beINvolved Student Orgs": "https://iub.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12122726"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_campuslabs
SUMMARY:Wilderness First Aid Courses
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260509T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260510T170000
UID:https://iub.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12122726
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://se-images.campuslabs.com/clink/images/3d
 e78e70-77dd-4d3a-b18e-a39aa078609deb51894f-9486-4bfa-b71e-954dccc1ec79.png
DESCRIPTION:Hosted by: Bradford Woods\n\nOur Wilderness First Aid (WFA) co
 urses will give you the skills needed to respond to medical emergencies wh
 en help is far away. This is a 2-day/16-hour course that features extensiv
 e hands-on learning opportunities. Students will walk away with a 2-year W
 FA certification from Stonehearth Open Learning Opportunities (SOLO)\, whi
 ch is one of the oldest wilderness medicine organizations in the world. St
 udents may also add on CPR modules and/or re-certify for their SOLO Wilder
 ness First Responder (WFR) certification. Courses start at $275. Cost incl
 udes course materials and lunch on Saturday and Sunday. Overnight lodging 
 from Friday&ndash\;Sunday may be available for participants on a first-com
 e\, first-serve basis. Register for the course here.
LOCATION:Bradford Woods
URL:https://iub.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12122726
X-SOURCE:IU beINvolved Student Orgs
END:VEVENT
