SUMMARY:Some Economics of the Social Safety Net
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260509T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260509T170000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020746Z
UID:e25935694006040900@facebook.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260509T140000
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260306T125958Z
DESCRIPTION:Over 40 million people in America receive SNAP (food stamp) be
 nefits\, over 70 million are enrolled in Medicaid\, and about 9 million re
 ceive Section 8 Housing Vouchers. Gerhard Glomm\, Professor of Economics\,
  will discuss some of the design features of these programs\, with an emph
 asis on relatively recent changes such as work requirements. He will then 
 share data on the costs and benefits of these programs. This event will be
  held at the Brown County Public Library\, 205 Locust Lane\, Nashville\, I
 N.\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/events/25935694006040900/
LAST-MODIFIED:20260306T130000Z
LOCATION:Brown County Public Library
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/25935694006040900/
END:VEVENT
