SUMMARY:Family Art Lab
DTSTART:20260510T170000Z
DTEND:20260510T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20251021T122032Z
UID:20260510T170000Z-2093916@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260510T170000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,402,390/26917_xxmarketing_arttherapyvideoshoot_072919_289
 _o4.rev.1751482406.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:Please note&#160\;that&#160\;this month's Family Art Lab does 
 not follow&#160\;the second Sunday schedule.  Designed for K-12 students a
 nd their families\, this event offers a fun and flexible way to spark crea
 tivity and connect with each other. All ages and experience levels are wel
 come!  Come and go at your own pace. We recommend planning for at least an
  hour to explore the gallery and make art.  Start in the Art Studio inside
  the Kimberly and John Simpson Center for Education on the museum's 2nd fl
 oor to pick up your Gallery Challenge. Then head to the galleries to find 
 the artwork we'll use as inspiration for our project! When you're ready\, 
 head back to the studio for our hands-on art-making activity that everyone
  will love.  This program takes place every Second Sunday of the month\, e
 xcluding holidays and museum closures. Each month features new artworks an
 d materials\, so there's always something fresh to explore and create!  Al
 l children must be chaperoned.Know Before You Go:Read about where to find 
 us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.Strollers are w
 elcome in the galleries. When carrying small children\, please keep them i
 n front of you.  To save time at the lockers\, avoid bringing backpacks or
  large bags.  When You Arrive:If you parked in the IMU parking lot\, Guest
  Services can validate your parking voucher for a discount.  Store any lar
 ge bags in the lockers behind the Guest Services desk.  Head upstairs to t
 he 2nd Floor and into the Simpson Center for Education to start.  When in 
 the galleries\, do not touch the artwork. Be mindful to keep body parts an
 d anything you're carrying at least 18" away from the art.  Photography is
  welcome! Just no flash or selfie sticks.
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260415T184801Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART - Room Number: Roehm Famil
 y Art-making Studio
URL:https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2093916-family-art-lab
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Please note</strong><span style="b
 ox-sizing: border-box\; margin: 0px\; padding: 0px\;"><strong>&#160\;</str
 ong>that<strong>&#160\;</strong>this month's Family Art Lab does not follo
 w</span>&#160\;the second Sunday schedule.</p><p>  Designed for K-12 stude
 nts and their families\, this event offers a fun and flexible way to spark
  creativity and connect with each other. All ages and experience levels ar
 e welcome!</p><p>  Come and go at your own pace. We recommend planning for
  at least an hour to explore the gallery and make art.</p><p>  Start in th
 e Art Studio inside the Kimberly and John Simpson Center for Education on 
 the museum's 2nd floor to pick up your Gallery Challenge. Then head to the
  galleries to find the artwork we'll use as inspiration for our project! W
 hen you're ready\, head back to the studio for our hands-on art-making act
 ivity that everyone will love.</p><p>  This program takes place every Seco
 nd Sunday of the month\, excluding holidays and museum closures. Each mont
 h features new artworks and materials\, so there's always something fresh 
 to explore and create!</p><p>  All children must be chaperoned.</p><p><str
 ong>Know Before You Go:</strong></p><ul><li>Read about <a class="external"
  href="https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/your-visit.html"><span data-con
 trast="none">where to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum
  guidelines</span></a><span data-contrast="auto">.</span></li><li>Stroller
 s are welcome in the galleries. When carrying small children\, please keep
  them in front of you.  </li><li>To save time at the lockers\, avoid bring
 ing backpacks or large bags.  </li></ul><p><strong>When You Arrive:</stron
