ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1799,1800/30822_Ecosystem_Management_3.rev.1775574776.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Participants will begin with a visit to Mulyana: Vital Ecosyst
 ems\, drawing inspiration from the exhibition's imaginative underwater wor
 lds. The group will then explore a campus stream to learn how freshwater m
 acroinvertebrates help scientists assess stream health. The program conclu
 des back at the museum with hands‑on artmaking\, inspired by the biodive
 rsity observed in the stream and the visual language of the exhibition.  T
 he program is free and open to all ages. Participants will meet at the blu
 e benches by the main museum entrance at the start of the program.  Please
  dress for the weather\; jackets and boots are recommended for those who w
 ould like to step into the stream. In the event of inclement weather\, out
 door activities will shift to an indoor program.&#160\;
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
LAST-MODIFIED:20260413T173752Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2260936-stream-to-studio-exploring-l
 ocal-waters-and
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Participants will begin with a visit to 
 <a href="https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/current/_feature-exhibi
 tions/2026-02-07-mulyana-vital-ecosystems.html" target="_blank" rel="noope
 ner"><em>Mulyana: Vital Ecosystems</em></a>\, drawing inspiration from the
  exhibition's imaginative underwater worlds. The group will then explore a
  campus stream to learn how freshwater macroinvertebrates help scientists 
 assess stream health. The program concludes back at the museum with hands
 ‑on artmaking\, inspired by the biodiversity observed in the stream and 
 the visual language of the exhibition.</p><p>  The program is free and ope
 n to all ages. Participants will meet at the blue benches by the main muse
 um entrance at the start of the program.</p><p>  Please dress for the weat
 her\; jackets and boots are recommended for those who would like to step i
 nto the stream. In the event of inclement weather\, outdoor activities wil
 l shift to an indoor program.&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>\n  Emily Zarse<br />\n  Public Experiences Ma
 nager<br />\n  eczarse@iu.edu\n</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-COST:Free
