BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/2101230-homeschool-day-america-250"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_eskenazi_museum
X-SOURCE:Eskenazi Museum of Art
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: America 250
DTSTART:20260514T140000Z
DTEND:20260514T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20251028T160000Z
UID:20260514T140000Z-2101230@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260514T140000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1600,1067/28801_xxmarketing_arttherapyvideoshoot_072919_2
 95_o3.rev.1761681573.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:Travel back in time with us to America in 1776 to meet George 
 Washington and see the Declaration of Independence up close. Together\, we
 'll explore the art and stories that shaped our nation's founding. Afterwa
 rds\, we'll create our own colonial-inspired artwork in the studio\, refle
 cting on the theme of "What America Means to Me."Know Before You Go:  Meet
  us on the 1st floor of the museum at 10 a.m. Together\, we'll drop off pe
 rsonal items in the Simpson Center for Education before exploring the gall
 eries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head ba
 ck to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! D
 on't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome. Chaperones requir
 ed. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 chi
 ldren.Parking Information:  The museum is in the pedestrian district of ca
 mpus with several parking options nearby. The Indiana Memorial Union lot (
 900 E. 7th Street) is just a 5-minute walk diagonal to the museum\, and vi
 sitors can receive 40% off parking validation at the museum's guest servic
 es desk. The East Garage (105 N. Eagleson Ave.) and Fee Lane Garage (709 N
