 cting on the theme of "What America Means to Me."Know Before You Go:  Meet
  us on the 1st floor of the museum at 1 p.m. Together\, we'll drop off per
 sonal items in the Simpson Center for Education before exploring the galle
 ries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head bac
 k to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! Do
 n't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome. Chaperones require
 d. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 chil
 dren.Parking Information:  The museum is in the pedestrian district of cam
 pus with several parking options nearby. The Indiana Memorial Union lot (9
 00 E. 7th Street) is just a 5-minute walk diagonal to the museum\, and vis
 itors can receive 40% off parking validation at the museum's guest service
 s desk. The East Garage (105 N. Eagleson Ave.) and Fee Lane Garage (709 N.
  Fee Lane) are also convenient\, about an 8–10 minute walk. Learn more a
 bout parking on the Bloomington campus here (https://parking.indiana.edu/f
 acilities/index.html).
