SUMMARY:Spring Moth Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260515T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260515T213000
DTSTAMP:20260421T020748Z
UID:3bq5voqlnvug97vr4s7ijjj1ik@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260515T200000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20251205T174650Z
DESCRIPTION:Registration fee $6/in-city\, $7/non-city. Register online by 
 May 13 at <a href="https://webtrac.bloomington.in.gov/webtrac/web/search.
 html?Primarycode=140016">https://webtrac.bloomington.in.gov/webtrac/web/se
 arch.html?Primarycode=140016</a>. For ages 10 yrs. and up.<br>Late spring-
 early summer is an excellent time to observe moths. These insects overwint
 er in a pupal case under the leaf litter\, and arise in the springtime as 
 beautiful moths. Spring is the season when you are most likely to find cec
 ropia and luna moths. Lets see what we can find! Participants should plan 
 to bring portable seating and a flashlight and be able to hike on a modera
 te trail.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251205T174651Z
LOCATION:Griffy Lake Nature Preserve\, 3400 N Headley Rd\, Bloomington\, I
 N 47408\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
