SUMMARY:Pollinator Habitat Workshop Day 2 of 2
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260516T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260516T104500
DTSTAMP:20260421T020748Z
UID:0hjhbp33a7qqsnnqgqu95dbq1g@google.com__20260516
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20251205T170614Z
DESCRIPTION:Participation is free but registration is required\; register 
 by April 27 online at <a href="https://webtrac.bloomington.in.gov/webtrac
 /web/search.html?Primarycode=140012">https://webtrac.bloomington.in.gov/we
 btrac/web/search.html?Primarycode=140012</a><br>For ages 15 yrs. and up.<b
 r>Learn how to restore pollinator habitat with the Bloomington Parks and R
 ecreation Urban Greenspace team and biologists from the US Fish and Wildli
 fe Service (USFWS) Partners for Fish and Wildlife (PFW) Program. Topics to
  be covered include site selection and design\, site preparation\, plant s
 election\, planting methods and maintenance\, pollinator ID\, and plant ID
 . The goal of this workshop series is to provide participants with the too
 ls and knowledge to transform small areas of unused land (e.g. home\, scho
 ol\, and church yards) into native pollinator habitat. Participants must c
 ommit to both workshop dates.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251205T170634Z
