DESCRIPTION:Explore an imaginative\, immersive installation that transform
 s the museum into a vibrant\, crocheted\, underwater ecosystem inspired by
  Indonesia's spectacular coral reefs. Explore colorful coral reefs\, playf
 ul fish\, and fantastical sea creatures — all meticulously hand-knit and
  crocheted. Read more about this featured exhibition. (https://artmuseum.i
 ndiana.edu/exhibitions/current/_feature-exhibitions/2026-02-07-mulyana-vit
 al-ecosystems.html)Step into the world of acclaimed photographer Rania Mat
 ar (b. 1964\, Lebanon)\, whose striking portraits document young women per
 sisting in uncertain times. Matar's lens highlights women's creativity\, s
 trength\, dignity\, and resilience—offering a powerful counter-narrative
  to the challenges of her country and region. Read more about this feature
 d exhibition (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/current/_feature-e
 xhibitions/2026-03-05-rania-matar-where-do-i-go.html).  &#160\;  Know Befo
 re You GoSpace is available for the first 12 people to check in with Guest
  Services on the day. Drop by the information desk on the first floor of t
 he museum when you arrive.A small handbag may be carried at your side. Bac
 kpacks and large bags will need to be stored before touring. Learn more ab
 outmuseum guidelines.If you park in the IMU parking lot\, Guest Services c
 an validate your parking voucher for a discount.Read aboutwhere to find us
  and where to park\,
LAST-MODIFIED:20260415T154339Z
LOCATION:Eskenazi Museum of Art - Room Number: Check in with Guest Service
 s on the first floor
