BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2212650-the-whole-world-in-a-book-celebrating-madeline", "IU Bloomington Libraries": "https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2212650-the-whole-world-in-a-book-celebrating-madeline"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2212650-the-whole-world-in-a-book-celebrating-madeline"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_arts_humanities
X-SOURCE:IU Arts & Humanities Institute, IU Bloomington Libraries
SUMMARY:The Whole World in a Book: Celebrating Madeline Kripke's Dictionar
 y Collection
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260521
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260522
DTSTAMP:20260413T103544Z
UID:20260421T040000Z-2266899@events.iu.edu__20260521
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/261/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,435,435/30106_kripke_livewhale_avatar.rev.1771332577.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:When Kripke died in 2020\, she left behind a remarkable collec
 tion of over 20\,000 dictionaries\, as well as a rich manuscript archive a
 bout dictionaries\, her life\, and her collecting. In 2021\, the Lilly Lib
 rary acquired the collection\, keeping it intact and available for all to 
 study. The spring 2026 exhibition The Whole World in a Book: Celebrating M
 adeline Kripke's Dictionary Collection shares some of the collection publi
 cly for the first time\, curated by IU Provost Professor of English Michae
 l Adams (https://english.indiana.edu/about/faculty/adams-michael.html) and
  Lilly Library Executive Associate Director Erika Dowell.  Madeline Kripke
  believed that dictionaries are an especially useful lens for observing cu
 lture. She focused on slang and other marginalized language\, and she char
 ted the roles of dictionaries in everyday life. She collected\, not merely
  to possess\, but to share what she saw with scholars and the public\, and
  The Whole World in a Book realizes her ambition to do so.  This exhibitio
 n is on display until July 24\, 2026. For the Lilly Library's daily hours\
 , please visit the website (https://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library).
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
LAST-MODIFIED:20260413T143544Z
LOCATION:LILLY LIBRARY
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2212650-the-whole-world-in-a-book-ce
 lebrating-madeline
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  When Kripke died in 2020\, she left behi
 nd a remarkable collection of over 20\,000 dictionaries\, as well as a ric
 h manuscript archive about dictionaries\, her life\, and her collecting. I
 n 2021\, the Lilly Library acquired the collection\, keeping it intact and
  available for all to study. The spring 2026 exhibition <em>The Whole Worl
 d in a Book: Celebrating Madeline Kripke's Dictionary Collection</em> shar
 es some of the collection publicly for the first time\, curated by IU Prov
 ost Professor of English <a href="https://english.indiana.edu/about/facult
 y/adams-michael.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Michael Adams</a> and
  Lilly Library Executive Associate Director Erika Dowell.</p><p>  Madeline
  Kripke believed that dictionaries are an especially useful lens for obser
 ving culture. She focused on slang and other marginalized language\, and s
 he charted the roles of dictionaries in everyday life. She collected\, not
  merely to possess\, but to share what she saw with scholars and the publi
 c\, and <em>The Whole World in a Book</em> realizes her ambition to do so.
 </p><p>  This exhibition is on display until July 24\, 2026. For the Lilly
  Library's daily hours\, <a href="https://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-libr
 ary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">please visit the website</a>.</p><p><p
