BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/1992757-placeholder-writing-in-the-galleries", "Eskenazi Museum of Art": "https://events.iu.edu/artmuseum/event/1992757-writing-in-the-galleries"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"IU Arts & Humanities Institute": "https://events.iu.edu/live/events/1992757-placeholder-writing-in-the-galleries"}
X-SOURCE-ID:iu_arts_humanities
X-SOURCE:Eskenazi Museum of Art, IU Arts & Humanities Institute
SUMMARY:Writing in the Galleries
DTSTART:20260606T170000Z
DTEND:20260606T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20250723T153202Z
UID:20260606T170000Z-1995878@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260606T170000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/29305_Writing_in_the_Galleries_-_thumbnail.rev.
 1767371047.jpg
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences,Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, we begin by looking closely at artwork—as
 king what we see\, think\, feel\, and wonder. Together\, we'll explore wha
 t we think the artist is trying to say and what the social significance of
  their message might be. Then we'll use our imaginations to respond to any
  aspect of our experience. Poets\, story-tellers\, and essayists are all w
 elcome in this group!  What to Bringyour favorite pencil (no pens).  a not
 ebook or paper. Clipboards are available to borrow.  a phone or camera to 
 take a picture of the art for later reference.  Know Before You GoArrive e
 arly\, check in\, and get ready for an on-time start.Readwhere to find us\
 , where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.About Your Facilit
 ator  Dedaimia Whitney earned an MFA in fiction from Indiana University un
 der the direction of Scott Russell Sanders. She taught creative writing at
  Franklin College for many years. She has served the museum as a docent si
 nce 2019. Her favorite works of art are those that are both visually stimu
 lating and thought-provoking.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260403T171349Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART - Room Number: Check in on
  the first floor
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/1992757-placeholder-writing-in-the-g
 alleries
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  In this workshop\, we begin by looking c
 losely at artwork—asking what we see\, think\, feel\, and wonder. Togeth
 er\, we'll explore what we think the artist is trying to say and what the 
 social significance of their message might be. Then we'll use our imaginat
 ions to respond to any aspect of our experience. Poets\, story-tellers\, a
 nd essayists are all welcome in this group!</p><h3>  What to Bring</h3><ul
 ><li>your favorite pencil (no pens).  </li><li>a notebook or paper. Clipbo
 ards are available to borrow.  </li><li>a phone or camera to take a pictur
 e of the art for later reference.  </li></ul><h3><strong><span data-contra
 st="none">Know Before You Go</span></strong></h3><ul><li data-leveltext="
