SUMMARY:Color Drawing and Painting Workshop
DTSTART:20260613T180000Z
DTEND:20260613T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260109T125303Z
UID:20260613T180000Z-2165253@events.iu.edu
RECURRENCE-ID:20260613T180000Z
ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/29093_Drawing_Workshop.rev.1763750697.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences,Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Discover the joy of drawing in an inspiring setting! Begin by 
 sketching directly from artwork in the collection to sharpen your eye and 
 strengthen your skills. Then\, move into the studio to learn about color t
 heory and add color to your artwork.Strengthen fundamental drawing skills 
  Explore color theory in action  Experiment with color media  Expand your 
 creative expression in a hands-on way  Reserve your spot. If this page say
 s\, "Registration has closed" that means the waitlist is full.SuppliesBrin
 g your favorite drawing pencil (e.g. 4B)\, a sketchbook or drawing paper\,
  and a phone or device to photograph artwork (without flash) as we sketch.
  Additional supplies are provided.  Know Before You GoArrive early to find
  parking\, check in\, and get your drawing supplies ready.  At 1:55 p.m. a
 ny unclaimed reservations will be released to guests who are standing by w
 aiting for a spot.  Where to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and
  museum guidelines (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/your-visit.html). 
  This workshop is recommended for ages 12 and up. Anyone under 18\, who is
  not an IU student\, must be accompanied by an adult.  When You ArriveChec
 k in with Guest Services at the information desk on the first floor\, even
  if you come often and even if you are late. We appreciate having an accur
 ate attendance count.  Store all backpacks and large bags before entering 
 the galleries. A small handbag may be carried at your side.  Get your supp
 lies ready. Attach an 18x24" piece of newsprint to a drawing board.  Cance
 llations  This workshop often has a waitlist. Please use the cancellation 
 link included with your confirmation email if your plans change.About the 
 Instructor  John Cheek has taught credit and non-credit classes for eight 
 years in portrait painting\, landscape painting\, palette knife painting\,
  life drawing\, beginning drawing\, and advanced drawing\, as well as in d
 esign. He volunteers his time and expertise to facilitate drawing workshop
 s at the Eskenazi Museum of Art.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260109T175303Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART - Room Number: Check in wi
 th Guest Services on the first floor
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2130634-color-drawing-and-painting-w
 orkshop
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Discover the joy of drawing in an inspir
 ing setting! Begin by sketching directly from artwork in the collection to
  sharpen your eye and strengthen your skills. Then\, move into the studio 
 to learn about color theory and add color to your artwork.</p><ul><li>Stre
 ngthen fundamental drawing skills  </li><li>Explore color theory in action
   </li><li>Experiment with color media  </li><li>Expand your creative expr
 ession in a hands-on way  </li></ul><p><span data-contrast="auto">Reserve 
 your spot. If this page says\, "Registration has closed" that means the wa
 itlist is full.</span></p><h3><strong>Supplies</strong></h3><ul><li>Bring 
 your favorite drawing pencil (e.g. 4B)\, a sketchbook or drawing paper\, a
 nd a phone or device to photograph artwork (without flash) as we sketch. A
 dditional supplies are provided.  </li></ul><h3><strong>Know Before You Go
 </strong></h3><ul><li>Arrive early to find parking\, check in\, and get yo
 ur drawing supplies ready.  </li><li>At 1:55 p.m. any unclaimed reservatio
 ns will be released to guests who are standing by waiting for a spot.  </l
 i><li><a href="https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/your-visit.html">Where 
 to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines</a>.  <
 /li><li>This workshop is recommended for ages 12 and up. Anyone under 18\,
  who is not an IU student\, must be accompanied by an adult.  </li></ul><h
 3><strong>When You Arrive</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>Check in with Guest
  Services at the information desk on the first floor\, even if you come of
 ten and even if you are late.</strong> We appreciate having an accurate at
 tendance count.  </li><li><strong>Store all backpacks and large bags befor
 e entering the galleries.</strong> A small handbag may be carried at your 
 side.  </li><li><strong>Get your supplies ready.</strong> Attach an 18x24"
  piece of newsprint to a drawing board.  </li></ul><h3><strong>Cancellatio
 ns</strong></h3><p>  This workshop often has a waitlist. Please use the ca
 ncellation link included with your confirmation email if your plans change
 .</p><h3><strong>About the Instructor</strong></h3><p>  John Cheek has tau
 ght credit and non-credit classes for eight years in portrait painting\, l
 andscape painting\, palette knife painting\, life drawing\, beginning draw
 ing\, and advanced drawing\, as well as in design. He volunteers his time 
 and expertise to facilitate drawing workshops at the Eskenazi Museum of Ar
 t.</p>
