CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:Look for your guide\, President George Washington\, as you dro
 p in to visit these three revolutionary destinations:The Lilly Library pre
 sents The Declaration of Independence: The Motives\, The Moment (https://l
 ibraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/declaration-independence).The Sidney an
 d Lois Eskenazi Museum of Art showcases George Washington's portrait by Gi
 lbert Stuart.  IU Auditorium is the caretaker of Thomas Hart Benton's icon
 ic murals (https://www.iuauditorium.com/about-us/benton-murals-organ-and-d
 ailey-art-collection)\, titled The Social History of Indiana.Spend an afte
 rnoon with us. Or a whole day. This self-guided offering is designed to al
 low you to create your own educational experience. Visit all locations in 
 one trip or come back to campus multiple times. Each Fine Arts Plaza desti
 nation has different operating hours\; please consult them carefully when 
 planning your trip. All locations are open Tuesday–Friday between 10 a.m
 . and 5 p.m.  Check our online event calendar at go.iu.edu/america-250 (ht
 tps://go.iu.edu/america-250) for special events and additional campus cele
 brations of America's 250th.  To schedule a tour for groups of students in
  grades 2-12\, see Field Trip Tours: Revolution &amp\; Reflection (https:/
 /artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/museum-tours/tour-types.html).&#160\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20260121T213518Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2176903-updated-revolution-refle
 ction-campus
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Look for your guide\, President George W
 ashington\, as you drop in to visit these three revolutionary destinations
 :</p><ul><li><strong>The Lilly Library</strong> presents <em><a href="http
 s://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/declaration-independence">The Decl
 aration of Independence: The Motives\, The Moment</a>.</em></li><li><stron
 g>The Sidney and Lois Eskenazi Museum of Art</strong> showcases George Was
 hington's portrait by Gilbert Stuart.  </li><li><strong>IU Auditorium</str
 ong> is the caretaker of <a href="https://www.iuauditorium.com/about-us/be
 nton-murals-organ-and-dailey-art-collection" target="_blank" rel="noopener
 ">Thomas Hart Benton's iconic murals</a>\, titled <em>The Social History o
 f Indiana.</em></li></ul><p><strong>Spend an afternoon with us. Or a whole
  day.</strong> This self-guided offering is designed to allow you to creat
 e your own educational experience. Visit all locations in one trip or come
  back to campus multiple times. Each Fine Arts Plaza destination has diffe
 rent operating hours\; please consult them carefully when planning your tr
 ip. <strong>All locations are open Tuesday–Friday between 10 a.m. and 5 
 p.m.</strong></p><p>  Check our online event calendar at <a href="https://
 go.iu.edu/america-250">go.iu.edu/america-250</a> for special events and ad
 ditional campus celebrations of America's 250th.</p><p>  To schedule a tou
 r for groups of <strong>students in grades 2-12</strong>\, see <a href="ht
 tps://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/museum-tours/tour-types.html">Field Trip
  Tours: Revolution &amp\; Reflection</a>.&#160\;</p>
