DESCRIPTION:Reserve your spot. If this page says\, "Registration has close
 d" that means the waitlist is full.SuppliesBring your favorite drawing pen
 cil (e.g. 4B)\, a sketchbook or drawing paper\, and a phone or device to p
 hotograph artwork (without flash) as we sketch.  Know Before You GoArrive 
 early to find parking\, check in\, and get your drawing supplies ready.  A
 t 1:55 p.m. any unclaimed reservations will be released to guests who are 
 standing by waiting for a spot.  Where to find us\, where to park\, access
 ibility\, and museum guidelines (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/your-
 visit.html).  This workshop is recommended for ages 12 and up. Anyone unde
 r 18\, who is not an IU student\, must be accompanied by an adult.  When Y
 ou ArriveCheck in with Guest Services at the information desk on the first
  floor\, even if you come often and even if you are late. We appreciate ha
 ving an accurate attendance count.  Store all backpacks and large bags bef
 ore entering the galleries. A small handbag may be carried at your side.  
 Get your supplies ready. Attach an 18x24" piece of newsprint to a drawing 
 board.  Cancellations  This workshop often has a waitlist. Please use the 
 cancellation link included with your confirmation email if your plans chan
 ge.About the Instructor  John Cheek has taught credit and non-credit class
 es for eight years in portrait painting\, landscape painting\, palette kni
 fe painting\, life drawing\, beginning drawing\, and advanced drawing\, as
  well as in design. He volunteers his time and expertise to facilitate dra
 wing workshops at the Eskenazi Museum of Art.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260109T165744Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART - Room Number: Check in wi
 th Guest Services on the first floor
