 \,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto">M
 ost of these materials originate from the collection of prolific miniature
  book collector\, Ruth Elizabeth Adomeit (1910-1996). Notable book artists
  highlighted in</span><i><span data-contrast="auto">Micro-Mythologies </sp
 an></i><span data-contrast="auto">include Maryline Poole Adams\, Carol Cun
 ningham\, Barbara J. Raheb\, Dianne Weiss\, and Gabrielle Fox.</span><span
  data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777
 215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><span data-contrast="auto
 "></span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;33555785
 6&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;:288}"></span></p><p><i><span da
 ta-contrast="auto">Micro-Mythologies: World Mythology Made Miniature </spa
 n></i><span data-contrast="auto">is curated by Curatorial Assistant Jake G
 entry\, with counsel from Sarah McElroy Mitchell\, Curator of Religious Co
 llections. In addition\, exhibition design was done by Jenny Mack and grap
 hic design by David Orr. This exhibition is on display in the Lilly Librar
 y Ball Room through December 2026.</span><span data-ccp-props="{&quot\;201
 341983&quot\;:0\,&quot\;335557856&quot\;:16777215\,&quot\;335559740&quot\;
 :288}"></span></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ALL-DAY:1
