ATTACH:https://events.iu.edu/live/image/gid/234/width/168/height/168/crop/
 1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/29093_Drawing_Workshop.rev.1763750697.png
CATEGORIES:Art and museum exhibitions,Lectures, talks, seminars, and confe
 rences,Training, non-credit classes, and learning opportunities
DESCRIPTION:Reserve your spot. If this page says\, "Registration has close
 d" that means the waitlist is full.SuppliesBring your favorite drawing pen
 cil (e.g. 4B)\, a sketchbook or drawing paper\, and a phone or device to p
 hotograph artwork (without flash) as we sketch.  Know Before You GoArrive 
 early to find parking\, check in\, and get your drawing supplies ready.  A
 t 1:55 p.m. any unclaimed reservations will be released to guests who are 
 standing by waiting for a spot.  Where to find us\, where to park\, access
 ibility\, and museum guidelines (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/your-
 visit.html).  This workshop is recommended for ages 12 and up. Anyone unde
 r 18\, who is not an IU student\, must be accompanied by an adult.  When Y
 ou ArriveCheck in with Guest Services at the information desk on the first
  floor\, even if you come often and even if you are late. We appreciate ha
 ving an accurate attendance count.  Store all backpacks and large bags bef
 ore entering the galleries. A small handbag may be carried at your side.  
 Get your supplies ready. Attach an 18x24" piece of newsprint to a drawing 
 board.  Cancellations  This workshop often has a waitlist. Please use the 
 cancellation link included with your confirmation email if your plans chan
 ge.About the Instructor  John Cheek has taught credit and non-credit class
 es for eight years in portrait painting\, landscape painting\, palette kni
 fe painting\, life drawing\, beginning drawing\, and advanced drawing\, as
  well as in design. He volunteers his time and expertise to facilitate dra
 wing workshops at the Eskenazi Museum of Art.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260109T165802Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART - Room Number: Check in wi
 th Guest Services on the first floor
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2130742-beginnerintermediate-drawing
 -workshop
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Reserve your spot. If this page says\, "
 Registration has closed" that means the waitlist is full.</p><h3><strong>S
 upplies</strong></h3><ul><li>Bring your favorite drawing pencil (e.g. 4B)\
 , a sketchbook or drawing paper\, and a phone or device to photograph artw
 ork (without flash) as we sketch.  </li></ul><h3><strong>Know Before You G
 o</strong></h3><ul><li>Arrive early to find parking\, check in\, and get y
 our drawing supplies ready.  </li><li>At 1:55 p.m. any unclaimed reservati
 ons will be released to guests who are standing by waiting for a spot.  </
 li><li><a href="https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/visit/your-visit.html">Where
  to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines</a>.  
 </li><li>This workshop is recommended for ages 12 and up. Anyone under 18\
 , who is not an IU student\, must be accompanied by an adult.  </li></ul><
 h3><strong>When You Arrive</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>Check in with Gues
 t Services at the information desk on the first floor\, even if you come o
 ften and even if you are late.</strong> We appreciate having an accurate a
 ttendance count.  </li><li><strong>Store all backpacks and large bags befo
 re entering the galleries.</strong> A small handbag may be carried at your
  side.  </li><li><strong>Get your supplies ready.</strong> Attach an 18x24
 " piece of newsprint to a drawing board.  </li></ul><h3><strong>Cancellati
 ons</strong></h3><p>  This workshop often has a waitlist. Please use the c
 ancellation link included with your confirmation email if your plans chang
 e.</p><h3><strong>About the Instructor</strong></h3><p>  John Cheek has ta
 ught credit and non-credit classes for eight years in portrait painting\, 
 landscape painting\, palette knife painting\, life drawing\, beginning dra
 wing\, and advanced drawing\, as well as in design. He volunteers his time
  and expertise to facilitate drawing workshops at the Eskenazi Museum of A
 rt.</p>
